window.REV_FLIP=window.REV_FLIP||{};window.REV_FLIP["langgraph"]=[{"id":"langgraph-f0001","card":"q-langgraph-001-overview","sec":"langgraph-s001","q":"What is the running example used to teach LangGraph in this course?","a":"<p>A laptop-company chatbot. It grows from a math ReAct agent into a Product Q&amp;A bot, a custom Orders agent, a reflection summarizer, and a router over several agents.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0002","card":"q-langgraph-001-overview","sec":"langgraph-s001","q":"Which agentic patterns does the LangGraph course build on top of ReAct?","a":"<p>Planning, Tool Use, Reflection, Routing and Multi-agent.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0003","card":"q-langgraph-001-overview","sec":"langgraph-s001","q":"In the LangGraph course, which code is treated as the canonical version when a notebook and a lesson file differ?","a":"<p>The notebook code is canonical. Lesson-file variants are noted only where they differ.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0004","card":"q-langgraph-002-1-setup-course-scope","sec":"langgraph-s002","q":"What is the goal of the LangGraph course?","a":"<p>Build agentic chatbots with LangGraph using prebuilt templates and custom graphs.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0005","card":"q-langgraph-002-1-setup-course-scope","sec":"langgraph-s002","q":"What are the prerequisites and the recommended environment for the LangGraph course?","a":"<p>Prerequisites: Python/Jupyter, generative AI, and LangChain chains and agents. Environment: GitHub Codespaces with Python 3.10.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0006","card":"q-langgraph-002-1-setup-course-scope","sec":"langgraph-s002","q":"In the LangGraph course, how do you open the environment in GitHub?","a":"<p>In the repository <code>build-ai-agents-and-chatbots-with-langgraph</code>, go to Code, then Create Codespace on Main. Python 3.10 is recommended.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code># Repository: build-ai-agents-and-chatbots-with-langgraph\n# Navigate to: Code → Create Codespace on Main\n# Python version: 3.10 (recommended)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0007","card":"q-langgraph-002-1-setup-course-scope","sec":"langgraph-s002","q":"Which versions of langchain, langgraph and langchain-openai do the LangGraph notebooks pin, and how are they installed?","a":"<p><code>langchain==0.3.12</code>, <code>langgraph==0.2.59</code> and <code>langchain-openai==0.2.12</code>, installed with <code>!pip install</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>!pip install langchain==0.3.12\n!pip install langchain-openai==0.2.12\n!pip install langgraph==0.2.59</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0008","card":"q-langgraph-002-1-setup-course-scope","sec":"langgraph-s002","q":"Which other packages does the LangGraph course pin for Chroma, PDFs and data?","a":"<p><code>langchain_chroma==0.1.4</code>, <code>pysqlite3-binary==0.5.4</code>, <code>pypdf==5.1.0</code>, <code>pandas==2.2.3</code>, plus <code>tenacity==9.0.0</code>, <code>langchain_community==0.3.12</code> and <code>nbformat==5.10.4</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>!pip install langchain_chroma==0.1.4\n!pip install pypdf==5.1.0\n!pip install pandas==2.2.3</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0009","card":"q-langgraph-002-1-setup-course-scope","sec":"langgraph-s002","q":"Which models does the LangGraph course use, and where do the credentials go?","a":"<p>Azure OpenAI: <code>gpt-4o</code> for chat and <code>text-embedding-3-large</code> for embeddings. Keep credentials in environment variables.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import os\nos.environ[&quot;AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY&quot;] = &quot;&lt;your-key&gt;&quot;\nos.environ[&quot;AZURE_OPENAI_ENDPOINT&quot;] = &quot;&lt;your-endpoint&gt;&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0010","card":"q-langgraph-002-1-setup-course-scope","sec":"langgraph-s002","q":"In LangGraph, how do you create the Azure chat model and the embedding model used in every later section?","a":"<p>Use <code>AzureChatOpenAI</code> for the chat model and <code>AzureOpenAIEmbeddings</code> for embeddings.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from langchain_openai import AzureChatOpenAI, AzureOpenAIEmbeddings\n\nmodel = AzureChatOpenAI(\n    azure_deployment=&quot;gpt-4o&quot;,\n    api_version=&quot;2023-03-15-preview&quot;,\n    model=&quot;gpt-4o&quot;\n)\n\nembedding = AzureOpenAIEmbeddings(\n    model=&quot;text-embedding-3-large&quot;,\n    openai_api_version=&quot;2023-05-15&quot;\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0011","card":"q-langgraph-002-1-setup-course-scope","sec":"langgraph-s002","q":"How do you load a <code>.env</code> file and turn on LangSmith tracing in the LangGraph course setup?","a":"<p>Call <code>load_dotenv()</code>, then set the API keys and <code>LANGCHAIN_TRACING_V2</code> to <code>\"true\"</code> in <code>os.environ</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import os\nfrom dotenv import load_dotenv\n\nload_dotenv()\n\nos.environ[&quot;LANGCHAIN_TRACING_V2&quot;] = &quot;true&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0012","card":"q-langgraph-002-1-setup-course-scope","sec":"langgraph-s002","q":"What is the lesson-file variant for creating <code>AzureChatOpenAI</code> in the LangGraph course?","a":"<p>Pass <code>azure_endpoint=</code>, <code>api_key=</code>, <code>azure_deployment=</code> and <code>temperature=0</code> directly to <code>AzureChatOpenAI</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0013","card":"q-langgraph-003-2-1-conversational-ai-and-chatbots","sec":"langgraph-s003","q":"What is conversational AI, and how does a chatbot relate to it?","a":"<p>Conversational AI simulates human conversation with natural language understanding, processing and generation. A chatbot is built on it to infer intent and respond.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0014","card":"q-langgraph-003-2-1-conversational-ai-and-chatbots","sec":"langgraph-s003","q":"What traits does a chatbot have?","a":"<p>Free-form text in and out, multi-language support, text, voice and multimedia, a persona and purpose, backend integration, conversational memory, and small-talk handling.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0015","card":"q-langgraph-003-2-1-conversational-ai-and-chatbots","sec":"langgraph-s003","q":"In the basic chatbot example, which class stores the conversation, and how does <code>chat</code> add messages to it?","a":"<p><code>ConversationBufferMemory</code> stores it. <code>chat</code> adds the user message and the AI response to <code>chat_memory</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from langchain.memory import ConversationBufferMemory\n\nself.memory = ConversationBufferMemory()\nself.memory.chat_memory.add_user_message(user_input)\nself.memory.chat_memory.add_ai_message(response)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0016","card":"q-langgraph-003-2-1-conversational-ai-and-chatbots","sec":"langgraph-s003","q":"In the basic chatbot example, how does <code>generate_response</code> handle greetings?","a":"<p>It checks whether \"hello\", \"hi\" or \"hey\" appears in the lower-cased input and returns a greeting that names the persona. Otherwise it returns a generic reply.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>if any(greeting in input_text.lower() for greeting in [&quot;hello&quot;, &quot;hi&quot;, &quot;hey&quot;]):\n    return f&quot;Hello! I&#x27;m your {self.persona}. How can I help you?&quot;\nreturn &quot;I understand your request. Let me help you with that.&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0017","card":"q-langgraph-004-2-2-agentic-ai","sec":"langgraph-s004","q":"What is agentic AI?","a":"<p>Generative AI that decides and acts autonomously toward a goal with minimal human intervention.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0018","card":"q-langgraph-004-2-2-agentic-ai","sec":"langgraph-s004","q":"What are the five agentic patterns, and what does each do?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Pattern</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Planning</td><td>Breaks a goal into steps</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Tool Use</td><td>Picks and calls a function or API</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Routing</td><td>Sends a request to the right handler</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Reflection</td><td>Reviews output and suggests improvements</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Multi-agent</td><td>Specialist agents cooperate</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0019","card":"q-langgraph-004-2-2-agentic-ai","sec":"langgraph-s004","q":"Give an example of each agentic pattern.","a":"<p>Planning: \"Create a marketing campaign\" becomes ordered steps. Tool Use: calculator, search, DB lookup. Routing: technical vs billing vs general. Reflection: a summary reviewer. Multi-agent: researcher, analyzer, writer.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0020","card":"q-langgraph-004-2-2-agentic-ai","sec":"langgraph-s004","q":"In LangGraph, how is a Planning pattern written as a node?","a":"<p>A node function asks the LLM to break the task into steps, returns the plan in state, and is added with <code>add_node</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def planning_node(state: AgentState):\n    task = state[&quot;messages&quot;][-1]\n\n    return {&quot;current_step&quot;: &quot;planning&quot;, &quot;result&quot;: plan.content}\n\ngraph.add_node(&quot;planner&quot;, planning_node)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0021","card":"q-langgraph-004-2-2-agentic-ai","sec":"langgraph-s004","q":"In LangGraph, how is a Tool Use pattern written as a node?","a":"<p>A node extracts a query, runs a tool such as <code>DuckDuckGoSearchRun</code>, and returns the result in state.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from langchain.tools import DuckDuckGoSearchRun\n\nsearch_tool = DuckDuckGoSearchRun()\n\ndef tool_use_node(state: AgentState):\n    query = extract_search_query(state[&quot;messages&quot;][-1])\n    result = search_tool.run(query)\n\n    return {&quot;result&quot;: result, &quot;current_step&quot;: &quot;tool_executed&quot;}\n\ngraph.add_node(&quot;search&quot;, tool_use_node)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0022","card":"q-langgraph-004-2-2-agentic-ai","sec":"langgraph-s004","q":"In LangGraph, how is a Reflection pattern written as a node?","a":"<p>A node takes the previous result from state, asks the LLM to evaluate it and suggest improvements, and returns the reflection.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def reflection_node(state: AgentState):\n    previous_result = state[&quot;result&quot;]\n\n    return {&quot;current_step&quot;: &quot;reflection&quot;, &quot;result&quot;: reflection.content}\n\ngraph.add_node(&quot;reflect&quot;, reflection_node)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0023","card":"q-langgraph-004-2-2-agentic-ai","sec":"langgraph-s004","q":"In LangGraph, how is a Routing pattern written?","a":"<p>A routing function returns a key based on the message, and <code>add_conditional_edges</code> maps each key to a node name.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>graph.add_conditional_edges(\n    &quot;router&quot;,\n    routing_condition,\n    {\n        &quot;search&quot;: &quot;search&quot;,\n        &quot;calculator&quot;: &quot;calculator&quot;, \n        &quot;general&quot;: &quot;general_agent&quot;\n    }\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0024","card":"q-langgraph-005-2-2-agentic-ai","sec":"langgraph-s004","q":"In the LangGraph multi-agent example, what does the shared state hold?","a":"<p><code>messages</code>, an <code>agent_results</code> dict, and <code>current_agent</code>. The coordinator picks the specialist, and each agent writes its own key in <code>agent_results</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>class MultiAgentState(TypedDict):\n    messages: List[str]\n    agent_results: dict\n    current_agent: str</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0025","card":"q-langgraph-005-2-2-agentic-ai","sec":"langgraph-s004","q":"In the LangGraph multi-agent example, what does the coordinator node do?","a":"<p>It classifies the task and sets <code>current_agent</code> to the task type.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def coordinator_node(state: MultiAgentState):\n    # Determine which agent should handle the task\n    task_type = classify_task(state[&quot;messages&quot;][-1])\n\n    return {&quot;current_agent&quot;: task_type}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0026","card":"q-langgraph-005-2-2-agentic-ai","sec":"langgraph-s004","q":"In the LangGraph multi-agent example, how does the analysis agent use the research agent's work?","a":"<p>The research agent stores its result under <code>agent_results[\"research\"]</code>. The analysis agent reads that key from shared state and asks the LLM to analyze it.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def research_agent_node(state: MultiAgentState):\n    result = search_tool.run(state[&quot;messages&quot;][-1])\n    return {&quot;agent_results&quot;: {&quot;research&quot;: result}}\n\ndef analysis_agent_node(state: MultiAgentState):\n    data = state[&quot;agent_results&quot;].get(&quot;research&quot;, &quot;&quot;)\n    analysis = llm.invoke(f&quot;Analyze this data: {data}&quot;)\n    return {&quot;agent_results&quot;: {&quot;analysis&quot;: analysis.content}}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0027","card":"q-langgraph-005-2-2-agentic-ai","sec":"langgraph-s004","q":"In LangGraph, how do you wire a multi-agent graph so a coordinator picks the specialist?","a":"<p>Add the nodes, add conditional edges from the coordinator that read <code>current_agent</code>, and set the coordinator as the entry point.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>multi_graph = StateGraph(MultiAgentState)\n\nmulti_graph.add_node(&quot;coordinator&quot;, coordinator_node)\nmulti_graph.add_node(&quot;researcher&quot;, research_agent_node)\nmulti_graph.add_node(&quot;analyst&quot;, analysis_agent_node)\n\nmulti_graph.add_conditional_edges(\n    &quot;coordinator&quot;,\n    lambda x: x[&quot;current_agent&quot;],\n    {&quot;research&quot;: &quot;researcher&quot;, &quot;analysis&quot;: &quot;analyst&quot;}\n)\n\nmulti_graph.set_entry_point(&quot;coordinator&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0028","card":"q-langgraph-006-2-3-agentic-chatbot-chatbot-module-agent","sec":"langgraph-s005","q":"What does an agentic chatbot combine?","a":"<p>A chatbot module and an agent module.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0029","card":"q-langgraph-006-2-3-agentic-chatbot-chatbot-module-agent","sec":"langgraph-s005","q":"What does the chatbot module provide, and what does the agent module provide?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Chatbot module provides</th><th>Agent module provides</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>UI and interaction, multimedia</td><td>Autonomous decision making</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Conversation memory and history</td><td>Tool use and integrations</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>24/7 availability, multi-language</td><td>Multi-agent coordination</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Application integration</td><td>Personalization, learning, action execution, self-reflection</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0030","card":"q-langgraph-006-2-3-agentic-chatbot-chatbot-module-agent","sec":"langgraph-s005","q":"What is the flow in an agentic chatbot, from the user to the backend?","a":"<p>Chatbot UI, then conversation memory, then the agent coordinator, then specialized agents, then backend systems.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0031","card":"q-langgraph-006-2-3-agentic-chatbot-chatbot-module-agent","sec":"langgraph-s005","q":"In the <code>AgenticChatbot</code> example, what steps does <code>process_message</code> take?","a":"<p>It stores the user message in memory, routes to an agent type, gets the agent's response using the context, stores the response, and returns it.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def process_message(self, user_input: str) -&gt; str:\n    # Store user message\n    self.memory.chat_memory.add_user_message(user_input)\n\n    # Route to appropriate agent\n    agent_type = self.route_to_agent(user_input)\n    agent = self.agents[agent_type]\n\n    # Get agent response\n    response = agent.process(user_input, self.get_context())\n\n    # Store response\n    self.memory.chat_memory.add_ai_message(response)\n\n    return response</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0032","card":"q-langgraph-006-2-3-agentic-chatbot-chatbot-module-agent","sec":"langgraph-s005","q":"In the <code>AgenticChatbot</code> example, how does <code>route_to_agent</code> choose an agent?","a":"<p>\"plan\" in the input goes to the planner. \"tool\" or \"calculate\" goes to the tool user. Anything else goes to the router agent.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def route_to_agent(self, input_text: str) -&gt; str:\n    if &quot;plan&quot; in input_text.lower():\n        return &quot;planner&quot;\n    elif &quot;tool&quot; in input_text.lower() or &quot;calculate&quot; in input_text.lower():\n        return &quot;tool_user&quot;\n    return &quot;router&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0033","card":"q-langgraph-006-2-3-agentic-chatbot-chatbot-module-agent","sec":"langgraph-s005","q":"In the <code>AgenticChatbot</code> example, what does <code>get_context</code> pass to an agent?","a":"<p>A dict with the conversation <code>history</code> (the memory messages), <code>user_preferences</code> and <code>session_data</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def get_context(self) -&gt; Dict:\n    return {\n        &quot;history&quot;: self.memory.chat_memory.messages,\n        &quot;user_preferences&quot;: {},\n        &quot;session_data&quot;: {}\n    }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0034","card":"q-langgraph-007-2-3-agentic-chatbot-chatbot-module-agent","sec":"langgraph-s005","q":"What is the enterprise agentic chatbot template, and how does it pick its agents?","a":"<p>A chatbot class that picks its agent set by domain. For <code>customer_service</code> it uses support, billing and technical agents. For <code>sales</code> it uses lead qualifier, product expert and pricing agents.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>if self.domain == &quot;customer_service&quot;:\n    self.agents = {\n        &quot;support&quot;: CustomerSupportAgent(),\n        &quot;billing&quot;: BillingAgent(),\n        &quot;technical&quot;: TechnicalAgent()\n    }\nelif self.domain == &quot;sales&quot;:\n    self.agents = {\n        &quot;lead_qualifier&quot;: LeadQualificationAgent(),\n        &quot;product_expert&quot;: ProductExpertAgent(),\n        &quot;pricing&quot;: PricingAgent()\n    }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0035","card":"q-langgraph-007-2-3-agentic-chatbot-chatbot-module-agent","sec":"langgraph-s005","q":"How does the enterprise chatbot process a query?","a":"<p>It selects a domain agent from the query and user context, then calls <code>process_with_context</code> on that agent.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>agent = self.select_domain_agent(query, user_context)\nresponse = agent.process_with_context(query, user_context)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0036","card":"q-langgraph-007-2-3-agentic-chatbot-chatbot-module-agent","sec":"langgraph-s005","q":"What are the success factors for an agentic chatbot?","a":"<p>A clear persona, robust memory, agent coordination, and tool integration.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0037","card":"q-langgraph-008-2-4-agent-state-vs-conversation-memory-f","sec":"langgraph-s006","q":"In LangGraph and agentic chatbots, what is the difference between agent state and conversation memory?","a":"<p>Agent state belongs to each agent, is created per prompt, and is discarded after the response. Conversation memory belongs to the chatbot, lasts the whole session, and is persisted.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0038","card":"q-langgraph-008-2-4-agent-state-vs-conversation-memory-f","sec":"langgraph-s006","q":"Who owns agent state, and who owns conversation memory?","a":"<p>Each agent owns its agent state, internally. The chatbot owns conversation memory.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0039","card":"q-langgraph-008-2-4-agent-state-vs-conversation-memory-f","sec":"langgraph-s006","q":"Is agent state shared between agents, and can conversation memory be?","a":"<p>Agent state is not shared between agents. Conversation memory can be passed to agents as input.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0040","card":"q-langgraph-008-2-4-agent-state-vs-conversation-memory-f","sec":"langgraph-s006","q":"What does agent state hold, and what does conversation memory hold?","a":"<p>Agent state holds the LLM execution plan, tools used with inputs and outputs, iterative planning steps, and custom data. Conversation memory holds all user prompts and responses, session metadata, and metrics such as accuracy, latency and relevancy.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0041","card":"q-langgraph-008-2-4-agent-state-vs-conversation-memory-f","sec":"langgraph-s006","q":"What is the lifetime of agent state in an agent?","a":"<p>It is created per prompt, query or goal and discarded after the response.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0042","card":"q-langgraph-008-2-4-agent-state-vs-conversation-memory-f","sec":"langgraph-s006","q":"In the <code>AgentState</code> dataclass example, which fields does the state have?","a":"<p><code>prompt</code>, <code>execution_plan</code>, <code>tool_calls</code>, <code>current_step</code> and <code>custom_data</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>@dataclass\nclass AgentState:\n    prompt: str\n    execution_plan: List[str]\n    tool_calls: List[Dict[str, Any]]\n    current_step: int\n    custom_data: Dict[str, Any]</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0043","card":"q-langgraph-008-2-4-agent-state-vs-conversation-memory-f","sec":"langgraph-s006","q":"In the <code>Agent</code> example, how is state created and discarded?","a":"<p><code>process_prompt</code> creates a new <code>AgentState</code> for the prompt, runs <code>execute_plan</code>, then sets <code>current_state</code> to <code>None</code> after completion.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>self.current_state = AgentState(\n    prompt=prompt,\n    execution_plan=[],\n    tool_calls=[],\n    current_step=0,\n    custom_data={}\n)\n\nresult = self.execute_plan()\n\nself.current_state = None</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0044","card":"q-langgraph-009-2-4-agent-state-vs-conversation-memory-f","sec":"langgraph-s006","q":"In the <code>ChatbotMemory</code> example, what does it track besides the conversation?","a":"<p>Session metrics: <code>start_time</code>, <code>total_prompts</code> and <code>avg_response_time</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>self.conversation_memory = ConversationBufferMemory()\nself.session_metrics = {\n    &quot;start_time&quot;: datetime.now(),\n    &quot;total_prompts&quot;: 0,\n    &quot;avg_response_time&quot;: 0\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0045","card":"q-langgraph-009-2-4-agent-state-vs-conversation-memory-f","sec":"langgraph-s006","q":"In the <code>ChatbotMemory</code> example, what does <code>add_interaction</code> do?","a":"<p>It adds the user prompt and the bot response to conversation memory, then updates the metrics: it increments <code>total_prompts</code> and updates the average response time.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>self.conversation_memory.chat_memory.add_user_message(user_prompt)\nself.conversation_memory.chat_memory.add_ai_message(bot_response)\n\nself.session_metrics[&quot;total_prompts&quot;] += 1\nself.update_avg_response_time(response_time)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0046","card":"q-langgraph-009-2-4-agent-state-vs-conversation-memory-f","sec":"langgraph-s006","q":"What does <code>get_context_for_agent</code> return in the <code>ChatbotMemory</code> example?","a":"<p>A dict with <code>conversation_history</code> (the messages) and <code>session_info</code> (the session metrics).</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def get_context_for_agent(self) -&gt; Dict:\n    return {\n        &quot;conversation_history&quot;: self.conversation_memory.chat_memory.messages,\n        &quot;session_info&quot;: self.session_metrics\n    }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0047","card":"q-langgraph-009-2-4-agent-state-vs-conversation-memory-f","sec":"langgraph-s006","q":"How do a chatbot and its agents coordinate memory and state?","a":"<p>The chatbot routes the request and hands each agent the conversation context. Each agent builds its own fresh state. The chatbot merges the answers and updates memory.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0048","card":"q-langgraph-009-2-4-agent-state-vs-conversation-memory-f","sec":"langgraph-s006","q":"If a chatbot handles three prompts, how many agent states and conversation memories result?","a":"<p>Three separate agent states and one shared conversation memory.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0049","card":"q-langgraph-009-2-4-agent-state-vs-conversation-memory-f","sec":"langgraph-s006","q":"In the <code>MultiAgentChatbot</code> example, how does <code>process_user_input</code> use agents and memory?","a":"<p>It routes to one or more agents, gets the context from memory, calls each agent's <code>process_prompt</code> (the agent creates its own state), combines the responses, then adds the interaction to memory.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>selected_agents = self.route_to_agents(user_prompt)\n\nfor agent_name in selected_agents:\n    agent = self.agents[agent_name]\n\n    context = self.memory.get_context_for_agent()\n\n    response = agent.process_prompt(user_prompt)\n    responses.append(response)\n\nfinal_response = self.combine_responses(responses)\n\nself.memory.add_interaction(user_prompt, final_response, response_time)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0050","card":"q-langgraph-009-2-4-agent-state-vs-conversation-memory-f","sec":"langgraph-s006","q":"In the <code>MultiAgentChatbot</code> example, how does <code>route_to_agents</code> choose agents?","a":"<p>If \"complex\" appears in the prompt, both agents run. Otherwise only <code>agent1</code> runs.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def route_to_agents(self, prompt: str) -&gt; List[str]:\n    if &quot;complex&quot; in prompt.lower():\n        return [&quot;agent1&quot;, &quot;agent2&quot;]  # Both agents\n    return [&quot;agent1&quot;]  # Single agent</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0051","card":"q-langgraph-010-2-5-langgraph-building-blocks","sec":"langgraph-s007","q":"What is LangGraph?","a":"<p>A workflow orchestration engine in the LangChain ecosystem for stateful multi-agent apps. It manages agent interactions and state, integrates LLMs, tools and third-party apps, and streams intermediate results.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0052","card":"q-langgraph-010-2-5-langgraph-building-blocks","sec":"langgraph-s007","q":"What kinds of nodes does LangGraph have?","a":"<p>An LLM node (analyzes the prompt and creates actions), a tool node (runs function tools), an action node (invokes other agents), and a logic node (custom code).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0053","card":"q-langgraph-010-2-5-langgraph-building-blocks","sec":"langgraph-s007","q":"What kinds of edges does LangGraph have, and what are Start and End?","a":"<p>Basic (sequential) edges and conditional edges (route on a check). Start and End blocks mark entry and exit.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0054","card":"q-langgraph-010-2-5-langgraph-building-blocks","sec":"langgraph-s007","q":"In LangGraph, what is agent state, and how does data move between nodes?","a":"<p>Agent state is a shared structure that nodes read and write. Data moves through state, not through edges.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0055","card":"q-langgraph-010-2-5-langgraph-building-blocks","sec":"langgraph-s007","q":"What does a generic LangGraph skeleton contain?","a":"<p>A <code>TypedDict</code> state, a <code>StateGraph</code>, nodes, edges, a conditional edge, and an entry point.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from langgraph.graph import StateGraph, END\nfrom typing import TypedDict, List\n\nclass AgentState(TypedDict):\n    messages: List[str]\n    current_step: str\n    result: str\n\ngraph = StateGraph(AgentState)\n\ngraph.add_node(&quot;agent&quot;, agent_node)\ngraph.add_node(&quot;tool&quot;, tool_node)\n\ngraph.add_edge(&quot;agent&quot;, &quot;tool&quot;)\ngraph.add_conditional_edges(&quot;tool&quot;, should_continue, {&quot;continue&quot;: &quot;agent&quot;, &quot;end&quot;: END})\n\ngraph.set_entry_point(&quot;agent&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0056","card":"q-langgraph-011-2-5-langgraph-building-blocks","sec":"langgraph-s007","q":"In LangGraph, how do you compile a graph and run it with an initial state?","a":"<p>Call <code>graph.compile()</code> to get an app, then call <code>app.invoke</code> with an initial state dict.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>app = graph.compile()\n\ndef run_agent(user_input: str):\n    initial_state = {\n        &quot;messages&quot;: [user_input],\n        &quot;current_step&quot;: &quot;start&quot;,\n        &quot;result&quot;: &quot;&quot;\n    }\n\n    result = app.invoke(initial_state)\n    return result[&quot;result&quot;]</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0057","card":"q-langgraph-011-2-5-langgraph-building-blocks","sec":"langgraph-s007","q":"In LangGraph, how can you wrap an agent run with error handling?","a":"<p>Wrap the call in <code>try/except</code> and return an error string.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def safe_agent_run(user_input: str):\n    try:\n        return run_agent(user_input)\n    except Exception as e:\n        return f&quot;Agent error: {str(e)}&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0058","card":"q-langgraph-011-2-5-langgraph-building-blocks","sec":"langgraph-s007","q":"In LangGraph, how can you add logging to a node?","a":"<p>Configure <code>logging.basicConfig(level=logging.INFO)</code>, get a logger, and log the current step inside the node.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import logging\nlogging.basicConfig(level=logging.INFO)\nlogger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n\ndef logged_agent_node(state: AgentState):\n    logger.info(f&quot;Processing: {state[&#x27;current_step&#x27;]}&quot;)\n    return state</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0059","card":"q-langgraph-012-2-5-langgraph-building-blocks","sec":"langgraph-s007","q":"In the <code>LangGraphMultiAgent</code> example, what is the flow between agents?","a":"<p>A sequential pipeline: <code>agent1</code>, then <code>agent2</code>, then <code>coordinator</code>. The entry point is <code>agent1</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>self.workflow.add_edge(&quot;agent1&quot;, &quot;agent2&quot;)\nself.workflow.add_edge(&quot;agent2&quot;, &quot;coordinator&quot;)\nself.workflow.set_entry_point(&quot;agent1&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0060","card":"q-langgraph-012-2-5-langgraph-building-blocks","sec":"langgraph-s007","q":"In the <code>LangGraphMultiAgent</code> example, which state keys do the agents write?","a":"<p><code>agent1</code> writes <code>agent1_result</code>. <code>agent2</code> reads it and writes <code>agent2_result</code>. <code>coordinator</code> combines both into <code>final_output</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>class MultiAgentState(TypedDict):\n    task: str\n    agent1_result: str\n    agent2_result: str\n    final_output: str</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0061","card":"q-langgraph-012-2-5-langgraph-building-blocks","sec":"langgraph-s007","q":"In LangGraph, how does a streaming node return intermediate results?","a":"<p>It uses <code>yield</code> to send partial results, such as the current step and a partial result, and returns a final result at the end.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>yield {&quot;current_step&quot;: f&quot;step_{i+1}&quot;, &quot;partial_result&quot;: result}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0062","card":"q-langgraph-012-2-5-langgraph-building-blocks","sec":"langgraph-s007","q":"In LangGraph, how do you use a LangChain retriever as a node?","a":"<p>Write a node that takes the last message as the query, gets relevant documents from the retriever, and returns their <code>page_content</code> in state. Then add it with <code>add_node</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def retrieval_node(state: WorkflowState):\n    query = state[&quot;messages&quot;][-1]\n    docs = retriever.get_relevant_documents(query)\n    return {&quot;retrieved_docs&quot;: [doc.page_content for doc in docs]}\n\nworkflow.add_node(&quot;retriever&quot;, retrieval_node)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0063","card":"q-langgraph-012-2-5-langgraph-building-blocks","sec":"langgraph-s007","q":"In the <code>LangGraphAgenticChatbot</code> example, what nodes and edges does the workflow have?","a":"<p>Nodes: <code>router</code>, <code>planner</code>, <code>executor</code> and <code>reflector</code>. The <code>router</code> goes to <code>planner</code> by a plain edge. The <code>planner</code> has a conditional edge: execute goes to <code>executor</code>, reflect goes to <code>reflector</code>. The entry point is <code>router</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>workflow.add_edge(&quot;router&quot;, &quot;planner&quot;)\nworkflow.add_conditional_edges(&quot;planner&quot;, self.should_execute, \n                             {&quot;execute&quot;: &quot;executor&quot;, &quot;reflect&quot;: &quot;reflector&quot;})\n\nworkflow.set_entry_point(&quot;router&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0064","card":"q-langgraph-012-2-5-langgraph-building-blocks","sec":"langgraph-s007","q":"In the <code>LangGraphAgenticChatbot</code> example, what does <code>chat</code> do around the workflow?","a":"<p>It builds an initial state with the user message, current step, agent outputs and conversation context, invokes the workflow, reads <code>final_response</code> from <code>agent_outputs</code>, and updates conversation memory.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>result = self.workflow.invoke(initial_state)\n\nfinal_response = result[&quot;agent_outputs&quot;].get(&quot;final_response&quot;, &quot;No response&quot;)\nself.conversation_memory.add_interaction(user_input, final_response, 0.5)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0065","card":"q-langgraph-013-3-1-what-react-is","sec":"langgraph-s008","q":"What does ReAct stand for, and where does it come from?","a":"<p>Reason + Act. It comes from a research paper. The LLM drives an iterative loop, which also makes agent actions explainable.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0066","card":"q-langgraph-013-3-1-what-react-is","sec":"langgraph-s008","q":"What is the ReAct loop?","a":"<p>User input, then Thought, then Action, then Observation, repeating until done, then the Final answer.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0067","card":"q-langgraph-013-3-1-what-react-is","sec":"langgraph-s008","q":"In ReAct, what happens in the Thought, Action and Observation steps?","a":"<p>Thought: the LLM analyzes the input and decides the next step. Action: the agent runs a tool or computation. Observation: the LLM checks the result and decides whether more steps are needed.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0068","card":"q-langgraph-013-3-1-what-react-is","sec":"langgraph-s008","q":"What is the math agent example in the course?","a":"<p>A ReAct agent with tools <code>find_sum</code> and <code>find_product</code>. \"What is the sum of 2 and 3?\" calls <code>find_sum(2, 3)</code> and returns 5.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0069","card":"q-langgraph-014-3-2-function-tools","sec":"langgraph-s009","q":"In LangChain, what does the <code>@tool</code> decorator do?","a":"<p>It turns a function into a tool automatically.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from langchain_core.tools import tool\n@tool\ndef find_sum(x:int, y:int) -&gt; int :\n    return x + y</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0070","card":"q-langgraph-014-3-2-function-tools","sec":"langgraph-s009","q":"Why does the docstring of a function tool matter in LangGraph?","a":"<p>The agent uses the docstring to discover what the tool does, its inputs and its outputs. Write it carefully.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>&quot;&quot;&quot;\nThis function is used to add two numbers and return their sum.\nIt takes two integers as inputs and returns an integer as output.\n&quot;&quot;&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0071","card":"q-langgraph-014-3-2-function-tools","sec":"langgraph-s009","q":"In the math agent, how is <code>find_product</code> defined?","a":"<p>With <code>@tool</code>, a docstring about multiplying two numbers, and <code>return x * y</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>@tool\ndef find_product(x:int, y:int) -&gt; int :\n    &quot;&quot;&quot;\n    This function is used to multiply two numbers and return their product.\n    &quot;&quot;&quot;\n    return x * y</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0072","card":"q-langgraph-015-3-3-prebuilt-react-agent-create-react-ag","sec":"langgraph-s010","q":"In LangGraph, how do you create a prebuilt ReAct agent for the math tools?","a":"<p>Call <code>create_react_agent</code> with the model, a system prompt in <code>state_modifier</code>, and the tool list.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from langgraph.prebuilt import create_react_agent\nagent_tools=[find_sum, find_product]\nagent_graph=create_react_agent(\n    model=model, \n    state_modifier=system_prompt,\n    tools=agent_tools)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0073","card":"q-langgraph-015-3-3-prebuilt-react-agent-create-react-ag","sec":"langgraph-s010","q":"What system prompt does the math ReAct agent use?","a":"<p>It tells the model it is a math genius, must use only the tools available, and must not solve the problem itself.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>system_prompt = SystemMessage(\n    &quot;&quot;&quot;You are a Math genius who can solve math problems. Solve the\n    problems provided by the user, by using only tools available. \n    Do not solve the problem yourself&quot;&quot;&quot;\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0074","card":"q-langgraph-015-3-3-prebuilt-react-agent-create-react-ag","sec":"langgraph-s010","q":"What does <code>create_react_agent</code> return in LangGraph?","a":"<p>A compiled LangGraph graph (<code>agent_graph</code>).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0075","card":"q-langgraph-015-3-3-prebuilt-react-agent-create-react-ag","sec":"langgraph-s010","q":"What is the input format of a prebuilt ReAct agent, and where is the answer?","a":"<p>Input is a dict with a <code>messages</code> list. The last message is the answer.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>inputs = {&quot;messages&quot;:[(&quot;user&quot;,&quot;what is the sum of 2 and 3 ?&quot;)]}\nresult = agent_graph.invoke(inputs)\nprint(f&quot;Agent returned : {result[&#x27;messages&#x27;][-1].content} \\n&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0076","card":"q-langgraph-015-3-3-prebuilt-react-agent-create-react-ag","sec":"langgraph-s010","q":"How do you print the step-by-step trace of a ReAct agent run?","a":"<p>Loop over <code>result['messages']</code> and call <code>pretty_repr()</code> on each message.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>for message in result[&#x27;messages&#x27;]:\n    print(message.pretty_repr())</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0077","card":"q-langgraph-015-3-3-prebuilt-react-agent-create-react-ag","sec":"langgraph-s010","q":"What message types appear in a ReAct agent trace, in order?","a":"<p><code>HumanMessage</code>, then <code>AIMessage</code> (tool choice and arguments), then <code>ToolMessage</code> (the result), then <code>AIMessage</code> (the final answer).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0078","card":"q-langgraph-015-3-3-prebuilt-react-agent-create-react-ag","sec":"langgraph-s010","q":"Which tools does the prebuilt agent call for \"What is 3 multipled by 2 and 5 + 1 ?\"","a":"<p>It calls <code>find_product(3, 2)</code> and <code>find_sum(5, 1)</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0079","card":"q-langgraph-016-3-3-prebuilt-react-agent-create-react-ag","sec":"langgraph-s010","q":"What does <code>debug=True</code> do in <code>create_react_agent</code>?","a":"<p>It prints the graph state per step, message IDs, LLM decisions, token usage, and tool inputs and outputs.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>agent_graph=create_react_agent(\n    model=model, \n    state_modifier=system_prompt,\n    tools=agent_tools,\n    debug=True)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0080","card":"q-langgraph-016-3-3-prebuilt-react-agent-create-react-ag","sec":"langgraph-s010","q":"What does the <code>custom_debug_analysis</code> helper do?","a":"<p>It counts the message types in the result, lists the tools used from the tool calls, and prints the total steps and the final answer.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>message_counts = {}\nfor msg in messages:\n    msg_type = type(msg).__name__\n    message_counts[msg_type] = message_counts.get(msg_type, 0) + 1\n\nprint(f&quot;Message breakdown: {message_counts}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0081","card":"q-langgraph-016-3-3-prebuilt-react-agent-create-react-ag","sec":"langgraph-s010","q":"In the <code>custom_debug_analysis</code> helper, how are tool calls extracted?","a":"<p>It loops over messages that have a non-empty <code>tool_calls</code> attribute and extends a list with them, then prints their names.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>tool_calls = []\nfor msg in messages:\n    if hasattr(msg, &#x27;tool_calls&#x27;) and msg.tool_calls:\n        tool_calls.extend(msg.tool_calls)\n\nprint(f&quot;Tools used: {[call.get(&#x27;name&#x27;, &#x27;unknown&#x27;) for call in tool_calls]}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0082","card":"q-langgraph-017-3-4-react-built-by-hand-what-the-prebuil","sec":"langgraph-s011","q":"What is the structure of a hand-built ReAct graph in LangGraph?","a":"<p>State holds the loop variables, there is one node per step, and a conditional edge loops observation back to thought until a final answer or the iteration cap.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0083","card":"q-langgraph-017-3-4-react-built-by-hand-what-the-prebuil","sec":"langgraph-s011","q":"What state does the hand-built ReAct agent use?","a":"<p>A <code>TypedDict</code> called <code>ReActState</code> with <code>messages</code>, <code>thought</code>, <code>action</code>, <code>observation</code>, <code>final_answer</code> and <code>iteration</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>class ReActState(TypedDict):\n    messages: List[str]\n    thought: str\n    action: str\n    observation: str\n    final_answer: str\n    iteration: int</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0084","card":"q-langgraph-017-3-4-react-built-by-hand-what-the-prebuil","sec":"langgraph-s011","q":"How does the <code>ReActAgent</code> class set up its LLM, tools and iteration limit?","a":"<p>It uses <code>ChatOpenAI</code> with <code>temperature=0</code>, a dict of tools by name from <code>math_tools</code>, and <code>max_iterations = 5</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>self.llm = ChatOpenAI(model=&quot;gpt-3.5-turbo&quot;, temperature=0)\nself.tools = {tool.name: tool for tool in math_tools}\nself.max_iterations = 5</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0085","card":"q-langgraph-018-3-4-react-built-by-hand-what-the-prebuil","sec":"langgraph-s011","q":"What does the thought node do in the hand-built ReAct agent?","a":"<p>It asks the LLM to analyze the request, with previous thought and observation as context after the first iteration, and decide the next action. It returns the thought and increments <code>iteration</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>thought = self.llm.invoke(prompt).content\nreturn {&quot;thought&quot;: thought, &quot;iteration&quot;: state.get(&quot;iteration&quot;, 0) + 1}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0086","card":"q-langgraph-018-3-4-react-built-by-hand-what-the-prebuil","sec":"langgraph-s011","q":"How does the action node in the hand-built ReAct agent pick a tool?","a":"<p>It checks the thought text: \"sum\" or \"add\" runs <code>find_sum</code>, and \"product\" or \"multiply\" runs <code>find_product</code>. It extracts numbers from the original message. Otherwise it returns \"No suitable tool found\".</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>if &quot;sum&quot; in thought.lower() or &quot;add&quot; in thought.lower():\n    numbers = self.extract_numbers(state[&quot;messages&quot;][-1])\n    if len(numbers) &gt;= 2:\n        result = self.tools[&quot;find_sum&quot;].func(numbers[0], numbers[1])\n        return {&quot;action&quot;: f&quot;find_sum({numbers[0]}, {numbers[1]}) = {result}&quot;}\n\nreturn {&quot;action&quot;: &quot;No suitable tool found&quot;}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0087","card":"q-langgraph-018-3-4-react-built-by-hand-what-the-prebuil","sec":"langgraph-s011","q":"What does the observation node do in the hand-built ReAct agent?","a":"<p>It asks the LLM whether the action result answers the original question completely. If the observation contains \"final answer\" or \"complete\", it extracts the final answer from the action result and stores it.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>if &quot;final answer&quot; in observation.lower() or &quot;complete&quot; in observation.lower():\n    final_answer = self.extract_final_answer(action_result)\n    return {&quot;observation&quot;: observation, &quot;final_answer&quot;: final_answer}\n\nreturn {&quot;observation&quot;: observation}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0088","card":"q-langgraph-018-3-4-react-built-by-hand-what-the-prebuil","sec":"langgraph-s011","q":"How does the hand-built ReAct agent extract numbers and the final answer?","a":"<p><code>extract_numbers</code> uses a regex <code>\\d+</code> and converts the matches to ints. <code>extract_final_answer</code> takes the text after the last <code>=</code> in the action result.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>numbers = re.findall(r&#x27;\\d+&#x27;, text)\nreturn [int(n) for n in numbers]</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0089","card":"q-langgraph-019-3-4-react-built-by-hand-what-the-prebuil","sec":"langgraph-s011","q":"How is the hand-built ReAct graph wired in LangGraph?","a":"<p>Nodes <code>thought</code>, <code>action</code> and <code>observation</code>. Plain edges go thought to action and action to observation. A conditional edge from observation goes back to thought or to END. The entry point is <code>thought</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>graph.add_edge(&quot;thought&quot;, &quot;action&quot;)\ngraph.add_edge(&quot;action&quot;, &quot;observation&quot;)\n\ngraph.add_conditional_edges(\n    &quot;observation&quot;,\n    should_continue,\n    {&quot;thought&quot;: &quot;thought&quot;, &quot;end&quot;: END}\n)\n\ngraph.set_entry_point(&quot;thought&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0090","card":"q-langgraph-019-3-4-react-built-by-hand-what-the-prebuil","sec":"langgraph-s011","q":"When does the hand-built ReAct <code>should_continue</code> end the loop?","a":"<p>When <code>final_answer</code> is set or <code>iteration</code> reaches <code>max_iterations</code>. Otherwise it returns \"thought\" to loop again.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def should_continue(state: ReActState) -&gt; str:\n    if state.get(&quot;final_answer&quot;) or state.get(&quot;iteration&quot;, 0) &gt;= agent.max_iterations:\n        return &quot;end&quot;\n    return &quot;thought&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0091","card":"q-langgraph-019-3-4-react-built-by-hand-what-the-prebuil","sec":"langgraph-s011","q":"How do you run the hand-built ReAct agent?","a":"<p>Build an initial state with the user message, empty strings and <code>iteration</code> 0, invoke the graph, and return <code>final_answer</code>, or \"Could not determine answer\" if empty.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>initial_state = {\n    &quot;messages&quot;: [user_input],\n    &quot;thought&quot;: &quot;&quot;,\n    &quot;action&quot;: &quot;&quot;,\n    &quot;observation&quot;: &quot;&quot;,\n    &quot;final_answer&quot;: &quot;&quot;,\n    &quot;iteration&quot;: 0\n}\n\nresult = graph.invoke(initial_state)\nreturn result[&quot;final_answer&quot;] or &quot;Could not determine answer&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0092","card":"q-langgraph-020-3-4-react-built-by-hand-what-the-prebuil","sec":"langgraph-s011","q":"What refinements does the course suggest for a hand-built ReAct agent?","a":"<p>Let the LLM choose the tool and parameters, plan up front for multi-step problems, and add error recovery.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0093","card":"q-langgraph-020-3-4-react-built-by-hand-what-the-prebuil","sec":"langgraph-s011","q":"How does the enhanced action node choose a tool?","a":"<p>It prompts the LLM with the request, the thought and the tool names with descriptions, and asks for the format <code>tool_name(param1, param2)</code>. Then it parses the decision and executes the tool.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>Which tool should be used and with what parameters?\nFormat: tool_name(param1, param2)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0094","card":"q-langgraph-020-3-4-react-built-by-hand-what-the-prebuil","sec":"langgraph-s011","q":"How does <code>AdvancedReActState</code> support multi-step problems?","a":"<p>It extends <code>ReActState</code> with <code>steps_completed</code> and <code>remaining_steps</code>. The thought node first creates a plan, then works through the next remaining step.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>class AdvancedReActState(ReActState):\n    steps_completed: List[str]\n    remaining_steps: List[str]</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0095","card":"q-langgraph-020-3-4-react-built-by-hand-what-the-prebuil","sec":"langgraph-s011","q":"How does the robust observation node handle errors in a ReAct agent?","a":"<p>If the action result contains \"error\", it sets an observation saying the action failed and a thought to reconsider the approach, which signals a retry. A raised exception sets an error observation and a final answer saying the task cannot be completed.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>if &quot;error&quot; in action_result.lower():\n    return {\n        &quot;observation&quot;: &quot;Action failed, need to try different approach&quot;,\n        &quot;thought&quot;: &quot;Previous action failed, reconsidering approach&quot;\n    }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0096","card":"q-langgraph-021-3-5-extending-batching-monitoring","sec":"langgraph-s012","q":"How do you add new tools to a prebuilt ReAct agent?","a":"<p>Add the tools to the list and update the system prompt.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>@tool\ndef find_difference(x: int, y: int) -&gt; int:\n    &quot;&quot;&quot;Calculate the difference between two integers (x - y).&quot;&quot;&quot;\n    return x - y\n\nextended_tools = [find_sum, find_product, find_difference, find_quotient]</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0097","card":"q-langgraph-021-3-5-extending-batching-monitoring","sec":"langgraph-s012","q":"How does the <code>find_quotient</code> tool handle division by zero?","a":"<p>It returns the string \"Error: Division by zero\" when <code>y</code> is 0. Otherwise it returns <code>x / y</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>@tool\ndef find_quotient(x: int, y: int) -&gt; float:\n    &quot;&quot;&quot;Calculate the quotient of two integers (x / y). Returns error if y is zero.&quot;&quot;&quot;\n    if y == 0:\n        return &quot;Error: Division by zero&quot;\n    return x / y</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0098","card":"q-langgraph-021-3-5-extending-batching-monitoring","sec":"langgraph-s012","q":"What does the extended math agent's system prompt tell the model?","a":"<p>It lists which tool covers each operation and ends with \"Always use tools, never calculate directly.\"</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>Always use tools, never calculate directly.</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0099","card":"q-langgraph-021-3-5-extending-batching-monitoring","sec":"langgraph-s012","q":"What is the caveat with the <code>calculator</code> tool that uses <code>eval</code>?","a":"<p><code>eval</code> on model output is unsafe. Use a real math parser.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>@tool\ndef calculator(expression: str) -&gt; str:\n    &quot;&quot;&quot;Evaluate mathematical expressions safely&quot;&quot;&quot;\n    try:\n        result = eval(expression)\n        return str(result)\n    except:\n        return &quot;Invalid expression&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0100","card":"q-langgraph-022-3-5-extending-batching-monitoring","sec":"langgraph-s012","q":"How does <code>safe_agent_execute</code> protect a ReAct agent run?","a":"<p>It invokes the agent in a <code>try/except</code>, returns the last message content if there are messages, returns a \"No response\" message if not, and returns an error string on an exception.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>if result[&quot;messages&quot;]:\n    return result[&quot;messages&quot;][-1].content\nelse:\n    return &quot;No response generated&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0101","card":"q-langgraph-022-3-5-extending-batching-monitoring","sec":"langgraph-s012","q":"How does <code>batch_process_questions</code> process several questions?","a":"<p>It loops over the questions, runs the agent on each in a <code>try/except</code>, and appends a result dict with the question, the answer or error, and a <code>success</code> flag.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>results.append({&quot;question&quot;: question, &quot;answer&quot;: final_answer, &quot;success&quot;: True})</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0102","card":"q-langgraph-023-3-5-extending-batching-monitoring","sec":"langgraph-s012","q":"How does <code>monitored_execution</code> measure agent performance?","a":"<p>It records the start and end time around <code>agent_graph.invoke</code> and builds metrics: <code>execution_time</code>, <code>message_count</code>, <code>final_answer</code> and <code>tool_usage</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>metrics = {\n    &quot;execution_time&quot;: execution_time,\n    &quot;message_count&quot;: len(result[&quot;messages&quot;]),\n    &quot;final_answer&quot;: result[&quot;messages&quot;][-1].content,\n    &quot;tool_usage&quot;: sum(1 for msg in result[&quot;messages&quot;] if &quot;ToolMessage&quot; in str(type(msg)))\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0103","card":"q-langgraph-023-3-5-extending-batching-monitoring","sec":"langgraph-s012","q":"How does <code>tool_usage</code> count tool calls in <code>monitored_execution</code>?","a":"<p>It counts messages whose type string contains \"ToolMessage\".</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0104","card":"q-langgraph-023-3-5-extending-batching-monitoring","sec":"langgraph-s012","q":"How does the <code>ReActMathChatbot</code> keep memory, and why does it not really work?","a":"<p>It keeps a manual <code>conversation_history</code> list. Each call sends only the new message, so \"multiply that result\" has no memory. Real memory needs a checkpointer and <code>thread_id</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>inputs = {&quot;messages&quot;: [HumanMessage(content=user_input)]}\nresult = self.agent_graph.invoke(inputs)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0105","card":"q-langgraph-024-4-1-design","sec":"langgraph-s013","q":"What is the Product Q&amp;A chatbot in the LangGraph course?","a":"<p>A self-service laptop chatbot that answers \"What are the features and pricing for X?\".</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0106","card":"q-langgraph-024-4-1-design","sec":"langgraph-s013","q":"What are the two tools of the Product Q&amp;A chatbot?","a":"<p>Function tool <code>get_laptop_price</code>: a DataFrame lookup (standing in for an RDBMS) from <code>data/Laptop pricing.csv</code> with columns <code>Name, Price, ShippingDays</code>. Retriever tool <code>get_product_features</code>: a PDF chunked and embedded into Chroma.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0107","card":"q-langgraph-024-4-1-design","sec":"langgraph-s013","q":"What are the agent and the chatbot in the Product Q&amp;A design?","a":"<p>The agent is a ReAct agent that chooses between the two tools. The chatbot is the agent plus conversation memory.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0108","card":"q-langgraph-025-4-2-function-tool-price-lookup","sec":"langgraph-s014","q":"How does <code>get_laptop_price</code> match a laptop name, and what does it return when nothing matches?","a":"<p>It does a prefix match on the name, case-insensitive. It returns <code>-1</code> when nothing matches.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>match_records_df = product_pricing_df[\n                    product_pricing_df[&quot;Name&quot;].str.contains(\n                                            &quot;^&quot; + laptop_name, case=False)\n                    ]</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0109","card":"q-langgraph-025-4-2-function-tool-price-lookup","sec":"langgraph-s014","q":"How does <code>get_laptop_price</code> return the price and handle no match?","a":"<p>It checks whether the matching DataFrame is empty. If empty it returns -1. Otherwise it returns the <code>Price</code> of the first match.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>if len(match_records_df) == 0 :\n    return -1\nelse:\n    return match_records_df[&quot;Price&quot;].iloc[0]</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0110","card":"q-langgraph-025-4-2-function-tool-price-lookup","sec":"langgraph-s014","q":"How do you load the laptop pricing data in the Product Q&amp;A chatbot?","a":"<p>With <code>pd.read_csv</code> into a Pandas DataFrame.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>product_pricing_df = pd.read_csv(&quot;data/Laptop pricing.csv&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0111","card":"q-langgraph-025-4-2-function-tool-price-lookup","sec":"langgraph-s014","q":"How do you test <code>get_laptop_price</code> as a plain function?","a":"<p>Comment out the <code>@tool</code> annotation, then call it with a name.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>#print(get_laptop_price(&quot;alpha&quot;))\n#print(get_laptop_price(&quot;testing&quot;))</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0112","card":"q-langgraph-026-4-3-retriever-tool-product-features-from","sec":"langgraph-s015","q":"What are the steps to build the product features retriever tool?","a":"<p>Load the PDF, chunk it, embed the chunks into Chroma, and wrap the retriever with <code>create_retriever_tool</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0113","card":"q-langgraph-026-4-3-retriever-tool-product-features-from","sec":"langgraph-s015","q":"How is the product features PDF loaded and chunked?","a":"<p><code>PyPDFLoader</code> loads it, and <code>RecursiveCharacterTextSplitter</code> splits it with <code>chunk_size=1024</code> and <code>chunk_overlap=256</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>loader=PyPDFLoader(&quot;./data/Laptop product descriptions.pdf&quot;)\ndocs = loader.load()\ntext_splitter = RecursiveCharacterTextSplitter(chunk_size=1024, chunk_overlap=256)\nsplits = text_splitter.split_documents(docs)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0114","card":"q-langgraph-026-4-3-retriever-tool-product-features-from","sec":"langgraph-s015","q":"How is the Chroma vector store created for the product features?","a":"<p>With <code>Chroma.from_documents</code>, passing the split documents and the embedding model.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>prod_feature_store = Chroma.from_documents(\n    documents=splits, \n    embedding=embedding\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0115","card":"q-langgraph-026-4-3-retriever-tool-product-features-from","sec":"langgraph-s015","q":"How is the retriever wrapped as a tool, and what does the description do?","a":"<p>Use <code>create_retriever_tool</code> with the retriever (<code>search_kwargs={\"k\": 1}</code>), a name and a description. The description tells the agent what the store holds.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>get_product_features = create_retriever_tool(\n    prod_feature_store.as_retriever(search_kwargs={&quot;k&quot;: 1}),\n    name=&quot;Get_Product_Features&quot;,</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0116","card":"q-langgraph-026-4-3-retriever-tool-product-features-from","sec":"langgraph-s015","q":"Why does the Chroma setup swap in <code>pysqlite3</code>?","a":"<p>It gives Chroma a new enough SQLite.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>__import__(&#x27;pysqlite3&#x27;)\nimport sys\nsys.modules[&#x27;sqlite3&#x27;] = sys.modules.pop(&#x27;pysqlite3&#x27;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0117","card":"q-langgraph-026-4-3-retriever-tool-product-features-from","sec":"langgraph-s015","q":"How does the lesson's product retriever setup differ from the notebook's?","a":"<p>The lesson uses <code>chunk_overlap=100</code>, <code>k=3</code> and an explicit <code>collection_name</code>. The notebook uses <code>chunk_overlap=256</code> and <code>k=1</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0118","card":"q-langgraph-026-4-3-retriever-tool-product-features-from","sec":"langgraph-s015","q":"How do you test the product feature store directly?","a":"<p>Call <code>invoke</code> on its retriever with a question.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>#print(prod_feature_store.as_retriever().invoke(&quot;Tell me about the AlphaBook Pro&quot;) )</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0119","card":"q-langgraph-027-4-4-agent-with-conversation-memory","sec":"langgraph-s016","q":"What is <code>MemorySaver</code> in LangGraph?","a":"<p>A checkpointer that stores graph state per thread ID. The same ID is the same conversation, so follow-ups resolve. A different ID is isolated.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0120","card":"q-langgraph-027-4-4-agent-with-conversation-memory","sec":"langgraph-s016","q":"What does the Product Q&amp;A system prompt do?","a":"<p>It sets the persona of a professional laptop chatbot, forces use of the available tools and not the model's own memory, and handles small talk and greetings professionally.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>To answer questions about laptops, you will ONLY use the available tools and NOT your own memory.\nYou will handle small talk and greetings by producing professional responses.</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0121","card":"q-langgraph-027-4-4-agent-with-conversation-memory","sec":"langgraph-s016","q":"How do you create the Product Q&amp;A agent with conversation memory?","a":"<p>Create a <code>MemorySaver</code> and pass it as <code>checkpointer</code> to <code>create_react_agent</code>, together with the model, tools and system prompt.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>tools = [get_laptop_price, get_product_features]\ncheckpointer=MemorySaver()\nproduct_QnA_agent=create_react_agent(\n                                model=model, #LLM to use\n                                tools=tools, #List of tools to use\n                                state_modifier=system_prompt, #The system prompt\n                                debug=False, #Debugging turned on if needed\n                                checkpointer=checkpointer #For conversation memory\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0122","card":"q-langgraph-027-4-4-agent-with-conversation-memory","sec":"langgraph-s016","q":"In LangGraph, which import gives you <code>MemorySaver</code>?","a":"<p><code>from langgraph.checkpoint.memory import MemorySaver</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0123","card":"q-langgraph-028-4-5-execution-streaming-vs-request-respo","sec":"langgraph-s017","q":"What is the difference between <code>stream</code> with <code>stream_mode=\"values\"</code> and <code>invoke</code>?","a":"<p><code>stream(..., stream_mode=\"values\")</code> yields the state after each step. <code>invoke</code> returns the final result.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0124","card":"q-langgraph-028-4-5-execution-streaming-vs-request-respo","sec":"langgraph-s017","q":"How do you give a LangGraph conversation memory when calling the agent?","a":"<p>Pass a config with a <code>thread_id</code>. Each user conversation uses a separate thread ID.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>config = {&quot;configurable&quot;: {&quot;thread_id&quot;: uuid.uuid4()}}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0125","card":"q-langgraph-028-4-5-execution-streaming-vs-request-respo","sec":"langgraph-s017","q":"How do you stream the agent's work step by step?","a":"<p>Loop over <code>agent.stream(inputs, config, stream_mode=\"values\")</code> and print the last message of each state.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>for stream in product_QnA_agent.stream(inputs, config, stream_mode=&quot;values&quot;):\n    message=stream[&quot;messages&quot;][-1]\n    if isinstance(message, tuple):\n        print(message)\n    else:\n        message.pretty_print()</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0126","card":"q-langgraph-028-4-5-execution-streaming-vs-request-respo","sec":"langgraph-s017","q":"In the multi-turn Product Q&amp;A conversation, which tool is used for greetings, features and \"How much does it cost?\"","a":"<p>Greetings use no tool. Names and features use the retriever. \"How much does it cost?\" uses memory plus the price tool.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0127","card":"q-langgraph-028-4-5-execution-streaming-vs-request-respo","sec":"langgraph-s017","q":"How do you run a multi-turn conversation on one thread?","a":"<p>Create one <code>thread_id</code>, loop over the user inputs, wrap each in a <code>HumanMessage</code>, call <code>invoke</code> with the same config, and print the last message.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>config = {&quot;configurable&quot;: {&quot;thread_id&quot;: str(uuid.uuid4())}}\nfor input in user_inputs:\n    user_message = {&quot;messages&quot;:[HumanMessage(input)]}\n    ai_response = product_QnA_agent.invoke(user_message,config=config)\n    print(f&quot;AGENT : {ai_response[&#x27;messages&#x27;][-1].content}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0128","card":"q-langgraph-028-4-5-execution-streaming-vs-request-respo","sec":"langgraph-s017","q":"How does the isolation test show that threads keep separate memory?","a":"<p>Two configs with different thread IDs each ask about a laptop, then both ask \"What is its price ?\". Each thread gets the price of its own laptop.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>config_1 = {&quot;configurable&quot;: {&quot;thread_id&quot;: str(uuid.uuid4())}}\nconfig_2 = {&quot;configurable&quot;: {&quot;thread_id&quot;: str(uuid.uuid4())}}\nexecute_prompt(&quot;USER 1&quot;, config_1, &quot;Tell me about the features of  SpectraBook&quot;)\nexecute_prompt(&quot;USER 2&quot;, config_2, &quot;Tell me about the features of  GammaAir&quot;)\nexecute_prompt(&quot;USER 1&quot;, config_1, &quot;What is its price ?&quot;)\nexecute_prompt(&quot;USER 2&quot;, config_2, &quot;What is its price ?&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0129","card":"q-langgraph-029-4-6-extras-from-the-lesson-file","sec":"langgraph-s018","q":"What is manual context injection, and when was it used?","a":"<p>Stuffing recent history into the prompt. It is the way to support follow-ups before the checkpointer.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0130","card":"q-langgraph-029-4-6-extras-from-the-lesson-file","sec":"langgraph-s018","q":"How does <code>contextual_chat</code> add recent history to the question?","a":"<p>It takes the last four history entries (the last 2 exchanges), builds a \"Recent conversation\" prefix, and puts it before \"Current question\".</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>recent_history = self.conversation_history[-4:]  # Last 2 exchanges\ncontext = f&quot;Recent conversation: {recent_history}\\n\\n&quot;\n\nenhanced_question = f&quot;{context}Current question: {user_question}&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0131","card":"q-langgraph-029-4-6-extras-from-the-lesson-file","sec":"langgraph-s018","q":"What does the <code>monitored_tool_execution</code> decorator do?","a":"<p>It wraps a tool function, times the call, and prints the tool name and the elapsed seconds.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>print(f&quot;Tool {tool_func.__name__} executed in {end_time - start_time:.2f}s&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0132","card":"q-langgraph-029-4-6-extras-from-the-lesson-file","sec":"langgraph-s018","q":"In what order do you apply the <code>monitored_tool_execution</code> decorator with <code>@tool</code>?","a":"<p><code>@monitored_tool_execution</code> goes on top of <code>@tool</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>@monitored_tool_execution\n@tool\ndef monitored_get_laptop_price(laptop_name: str) -&gt; str:</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0133","card":"q-langgraph-030-4-6-extras-from-the-lesson-file","sec":"langgraph-s018","q":"In the Product Q&amp;A chatbot, how do you test the tools alone?","a":"<p>Test the tools alone first, before the agent. Retriever tools take <code>.invoke({\"query\": ...})</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>price_result = get_laptop_price(&quot;MacRight&quot;)\nfeature_result = get_product_features.invoke({&quot;query&quot;: &quot;MacRight specifications&quot;})</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0134","card":"q-langgraph-030-4-6-extras-from-the-lesson-file","sec":"langgraph-s018","q":"How does <code>ProductChatbotService</code> create a session?","a":"<p>It makes a UUID session ID, builds a <code>thread_id</code> from it, and stores user ID, thread ID, creation time and message count under the session ID.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>session_id = str(uuid.uuid4())\nthread_id = f&quot;thread_{session_id}&quot;\n\nself.sessions[session_id] = {\n    &quot;user_id&quot;: user_id,\n    &quot;thread_id&quot;: thread_id,\n    &quot;created_at&quot;: datetime.now(),\n    &quot;message_count&quot;: 0\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0135","card":"q-langgraph-030-4-6-extras-from-the-lesson-file","sec":"langgraph-s018","q":"How does <code>ProductChatbotService.chat</code> keep each user's memory separate?","a":"<p>It looks up the session, builds a config from the session's <code>thread_id</code>, invokes the chatbot with it, and increments the message count. An unknown session returns an error.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>if session_id not in self.sessions:\n    return {&quot;error&quot;: &quot;Invalid session&quot;}\n\nsession = self.sessions[session_id]\nconfig = create_config(session[&quot;thread_id&quot;])</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0136","card":"q-langgraph-030-4-6-extras-from-the-lesson-file","sec":"langgraph-s018","q":"What does <code>create_config(thread_id)</code> return?","a":"<p><code>{\"configurable\": {\"thread_id\": thread_id}}</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0137","card":"q-langgraph-031-5-1-when-to-build-a-custom-graph","sec":"langgraph-s019","q":"When should you build your own <code>StateGraph</code> instead of <code>create_react_agent</code>?","a":"<p>When you need control over nodes, edges, state and routing. <code>create_react_agent</code> is only a ready-made graph.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0138","card":"q-langgraph-031-5-1-when-to-build-a-custom-graph","sec":"langgraph-s019","q":"How do nodes communicate in a custom LangGraph graph?","a":"<p>Through agent state, not edges.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0139","card":"q-langgraph-031-5-1-when-to-build-a-custom-graph","sec":"langgraph-s019","q":"What is the Orders chatbot use case?","a":"<p>A chatbot over <code>data/Laptop Orders.csv</code> (columns <code>Order ID, Product Ordered, Quantity Ordered, Delivery Date</code>) that gets order details and updates quantities. A DataFrame stands in for an RDBMS.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0140","card":"q-langgraph-031-5-1-when-to-build-a-custom-graph","sec":"langgraph-s019","q":"What is the graph of the custom Orders agent?","a":"<p><code>orders_llm</code>, then a conditional edge that asks whether there is a tool call. Yes goes to <code>orders_tools</code> and back to <code>orders_llm</code>. No goes to END. The LLM loops until it answers without a tool call.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0141","card":"q-langgraph-032-5-2-tools","sec":"langgraph-s020","q":"What does <code>get_order_details</code> do?","a":"<p>It does an exact match on the order ID. If found, it returns the product ordered, quantity ordered and delivery date. If not found, it returns <code>-1</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>match_order_df = product_orders_df[\n                    product_orders_df[&quot;Order ID&quot;] == order_id ]\nif len(match_order_df) == 0 :\n    return -1\nelse:\n    return match_order_df.iloc[0].to_dict()</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0142","card":"q-langgraph-032-5-2-tools","sec":"langgraph-s020","q":"What does <code>update_quantity</code> do?","a":"<p>It updates the quantity ordered for a given order ID and returns <code>True</code>. If no order matches, it returns <code>-1</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>product_orders_df.loc[\n    product_orders_df[&quot;Order ID&quot;] == order_id, \n        &quot;Quantity Ordered&quot;] = new_quantity\nreturn True</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0143","card":"q-langgraph-032-5-2-tools","sec":"langgraph-s020","q":"What do both Orders tools return when the order ID is not found?","a":"<p><code>-1</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0144","card":"q-langgraph-032-5-2-tools","sec":"langgraph-s020","q":"How do you load the orders data?","a":"<p>With <code>pd.read_csv</code> on <code>data/Laptop Orders.csv</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>product_orders_df = pd.read_csv(&quot;data/Laptop Orders.csv&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0145","card":"q-langgraph-033-5-3-the-custom-agent-native-tool-calling","sec":"langgraph-s021","q":"What is the state of the custom Orders agent, and what does <code>operator.add</code> do?","a":"<p>The state is <code>Annotated[list[AnyMessage], operator.add]</code>. The <code>operator.add</code> reducer appends each node's returned messages instead of overwriting.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>class OrdersAgentState(TypedDict):\n    messages: Annotated[list[AnyMessage], operator.add]</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0146","card":"q-langgraph-033-5-3-the-custom-agent-native-tool-calling","sec":"langgraph-s021","q":"What does <code>model.bind_tools(tools)</code> do?","a":"<p>It lets the LLM emit structured <code>tool_calls</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>self.model=model.bind_tools(tools)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0147","card":"q-langgraph-033-5-3-the-custom-agent-native-tool-calling","sec":"langgraph-s021","q":"What is <code>is_tool_call</code> in the custom Orders agent?","a":"<p>The conditional edge function. It returns <code>True</code> if the last message has tool calls, and the mapping <code>{True: \"orders_tools\", False: END}</code> routes the result.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>agent_graph.add_conditional_edges(\n    &quot;orders_llm&quot;,\n    self.is_tool_call,\n    {True: &quot;orders_tools&quot;, False: END }\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0148","card":"q-langgraph-033-5-3-the-custom-agent-native-tool-calling","sec":"langgraph-s021","q":"Why does <code>call_tools</code> wrap each result in a <code>ToolMessage</code> with <code>tool_call_id</code>?","a":"<p>The <code>tool_call_id</code> matches each result to its request.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>results.append(ToolMessage(tool_call_id=tool[&#x27;id&#x27;], \n                           name=tool[&#x27;name&#x27;], \n                           content=str(result)))</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0149","card":"q-langgraph-033-5-3-the-custom-agent-native-tool-calling","sec":"langgraph-s021","q":"Where does the custom Orders agent put its system prompt?","a":"<p>It is prepended to the messages on every LLM call, not stored in state.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>if self.system_prompt:\n    messages = [SystemMessage(content=self.system_prompt)] + messages</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0150","card":"q-langgraph-033-5-3-the-custom-agent-native-tool-calling","sec":"langgraph-s021","q":"How does the custom Orders agent get per-thread memory?","a":"<p>It compiles the graph with <code>checkpointer=MemorySaver()</code>, which gives memory per <code>thread_id</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>self.memory=MemorySaver()\nself.agent_graph = agent_graph.compile(checkpointer=self.memory)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0151","card":"q-langgraph-034-5-3-the-custom-agent-native-tool-calling","sec":"langgraph-s021","q":"How does the custom Orders agent graph set up its nodes and edges?","a":"<p>Nodes <code>orders_llm</code> and <code>orders_tools</code>, a conditional edge from <code>orders_llm</code>, a plain edge from <code>orders_tools</code> back to <code>orders_llm</code>, and <code>orders_llm</code> as entry point.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>agent_graph=StateGraph(OrdersAgentState)\nagent_graph.add_node(&quot;orders_llm&quot;,self.call_llm)\nagent_graph.add_node(&quot;orders_tools&quot;,self.call_tools)\nagent_graph.add_edge(&quot;orders_tools&quot;,&quot;orders_llm&quot;)\nagent_graph.set_entry_point(&quot;orders_llm&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0152","card":"q-langgraph-034-5-3-the-custom-agent-native-tool-calling","sec":"langgraph-s021","q":"How does <code>call_llm</code> work in the custom Orders agent?","a":"<p>It prepends the system prompt, invokes the model with the message history, and returns the result as a one-item messages list.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>result = self.model.invoke(messages)\nreturn { &quot;messages&quot;:[result] }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0153","card":"q-langgraph-034-5-3-the-custom-agent-native-tool-calling","sec":"langgraph-s021","q":"How does <code>call_tools</code> handle an unknown tool name?","a":"<p>It sets the result to \"Invalid tool found. Please retry\".</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>if not tool[&quot;name&quot;] in self.tools:\n    print(f&quot;Unknown tool name {tool}&quot;)\n    result = &quot;Invalid tool found. Please retry&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0154","card":"q-langgraph-034-5-3-the-custom-agent-native-tool-calling","sec":"langgraph-s021","q":"How does <code>call_tools</code> execute a tool call?","a":"<p>It looks up the tool by name in a dict and invokes it with the call's args.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>self.tools = { tool.name : tool for tool in tools }\nresult=self.tools[tool[&quot;name&quot;]].invoke(tool[&quot;args&quot;])</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0155","card":"q-langgraph-034-5-3-the-custom-agent-native-tool-calling","sec":"langgraph-s021","q":"What is the bug in the notebook's <code>call_tools</code>?","a":"<p>The <code>return</code> sits inside the <code>for</code> loop, so only the first tool call per turn runs. Dedent it to handle several.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0156","card":"q-langgraph-034-5-3-the-custom-agent-native-tool-calling","sec":"langgraph-s021","q":"What does the Orders system prompt tell the model?","a":"<p>It manages orders for laptops, uses the tools to get order details and update quantity, must not reveal information about other orders than the one requested, and handles small talk professionally.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>Do NOT reveal information about other orders than the one requested.</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0157","card":"q-langgraph-034-5-3-the-custom-agent-native-tool-calling","sec":"langgraph-s021","q":"How do you create the custom Orders agent and show its graph?","a":"<p>Pass the model, the two tools, the system prompt and <code>debug</code>, then draw the graph as an image.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>orders_agent = OrdersAgent(model, \n                           [get_order_details, update_quantity], \n                           system_prompt,\n                           debug=False)\nImage(orders_agent.agent_graph.get_graph().draw_mermaid_png())</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0158","card":"q-langgraph-034-5-3-the-custom-agent-native-tool-calling","sec":"langgraph-s021","q":"Why is the Orders system prompt a plain string in the custom agent?","a":"<p>The model init only accepts a string.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0159","card":"q-langgraph-035-5-3-the-custom-agent-native-tool-calling","sec":"langgraph-s021","q":"What does the Orders conversation test cover on one thread?","a":"<p>A greeting, an order lookup, an update (\"add one more\" needs memory), a re-check, a missing order <code>ORD-9999</code>, and a goodbye.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>user_inputs = [\n    &quot;How are you doing?&quot;,\n    &quot;Please show me the details of the order ORD-7311&quot;,\n    &quot;Can you add one more of that laptop to the order? &quot;,\n    &quot;Can you show me the details again ? &quot;,\n    &quot;What about order ORD-9999 ?&quot;,\n    &quot;Bye&quot;\n]</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0160","card":"q-langgraph-035-5-3-the-custom-agent-native-tool-calling","sec":"langgraph-s021","q":"How do you invoke the custom Orders agent in a conversation?","a":"<p>Call <code>orders_agent.agent_graph.invoke</code> with the user message and the thread config.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>ai_response = orders_agent.agent_graph.invoke(user_message,config=config)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0161","card":"q-langgraph-036-5-4-extras-from-the-lesson-file","sec":"langgraph-s022","q":"How do you inspect the saved state of a LangGraph thread?","a":"<p>Call <code>get_state(config)</code> on the graph. It returns a snapshot, and <code>.values</code> holds the messages.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>config = {&quot;configurable&quot;: {&quot;thread_id&quot;: thread_id}}\nstate = orders_agent.compiled_graph.get_state(config)\nmessages = state.values.get(&quot;messages&quot;, [])</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0162","card":"q-langgraph-036-5-4-extras-from-the-lesson-file","sec":"langgraph-s022","q":"What does <code>analyze_conversation</code> count?","a":"<p>User messages, AI messages, tool messages, the tools used and the tool usage count.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>user_messages = sum(1 for msg in messages if isinstance(msg, HumanMessage))\nai_messages = sum(1 for msg in messages if hasattr(msg, &#x27;tool_calls&#x27;))\ntool_messages = len(messages) - user_messages - ai_messages</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0163","card":"q-langgraph-036-5-4-extras-from-the-lesson-file","sec":"langgraph-s022","q":"What is the difference in the compiled graph name between the lesson and the notebook?","a":"<p>The lesson calls it <code>compiled_graph</code>. The notebook calls it <code>agent_graph</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0164","card":"q-langgraph-037-5-4-extras-from-the-lesson-file","sec":"langgraph-s022","q":"What is the alternative to <code>bind_tools</code> in the lesson, and why prefer native tool calling?","a":"<p>Parsing tool calls out of plain LLM text. It is brittle (regex on free text), so prefer native tool calling.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0165","card":"q-langgraph-037-5-4-extras-from-the-lesson-file","sec":"langgraph-s022","q":"What state does the text-parsing Orders agent use?","a":"<p><code>OrdersState</code> with <code>messages</code>, <code>llm_output</code>, <code>tool_calls</code>, <code>tool_results</code>, <code>final_answer</code> and <code>iteration</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>class OrdersState(TypedDict):\n    messages: List[str]\n    llm_output: str\n    tool_calls: List[Dict[str, Any]]\n    tool_results: List[str]\n    final_answer: str\n    iteration: int</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0166","card":"q-langgraph-037-5-4-extras-from-the-lesson-file","sec":"langgraph-s022","q":"How does the text-parsing Orders agent extract a tool parameter?","a":"<p>It uses a regex that matches the tool name followed by parentheses and takes the group inside, stripping quotes.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>pattern = f&quot;{tool_name}\\\\(([^)]+)\\\\)&quot;\nmatch = re.search(pattern, text)\nreturn match.group(1).strip(&#x27;&quot;\\&#x27;&#x27;) if match else None</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0167","card":"q-langgraph-037-5-4-extras-from-the-lesson-file","sec":"langgraph-s022","q":"How does the text-parsing agent extract the parameters of <code>update_quantity</code>?","a":"<p>It uses a regex that matches the order ID and a number, and returns them as a tuple.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>pattern = r&quot;update_quantity\\(([^,]+),\\s*(\\d+)\\)&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0168","card":"q-langgraph-038-5-4-extras-from-the-lesson-file","sec":"langgraph-s022","q":"How does the text-parsing Orders graph decide whether to call a tool?","a":"<p><code>should_call_tool</code> returns \"tools\" if the LLM output mentions <code>get_order_details</code> or <code>update_quantity</code>. Otherwise it returns \"end\".</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>if any(tool_name in llm_output for tool_name in [&quot;get_order_details&quot;, &quot;update_quantity&quot;]):\n    return &quot;tools&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0169","card":"q-langgraph-038-5-4-extras-from-the-lesson-file","sec":"langgraph-s022","q":"How is the text-parsing Orders graph wired?","a":"<p>Conditional edges from <code>orders_llm</code> map \"tools\" to <code>orders_tools</code> and \"end\" to END. A plain edge goes from <code>orders_tools</code> back to <code>orders_llm</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>graph.add_conditional_edges(\n    &quot;orders_llm&quot;,\n    should_call_tool,\n    {\n        &quot;tools&quot;: &quot;orders_tools&quot;,\n        &quot;end&quot;: END\n    }\n)\n\ngraph.add_edge(&quot;orders_tools&quot;, &quot;orders_llm&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0170","card":"q-langgraph-039-6-1-design","sec":"langgraph-s023","q":"What is reflection in agentic AI?","a":"<p>One LLM role generates and another reviews, and the output is refined from the critique: generate, review, regenerate, with an iteration cap.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0171","card":"q-langgraph-039-6-1-design","sec":"langgraph-s023","q":"What does the summarizer node do in the reflection graph?","a":"<p>It writes the summary and revises it when review comments or user critique are in the history. It is the entry point.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0172","card":"q-langgraph-039-6-1-design","sec":"langgraph-s023","q":"What does the reviewer node do in the reflection graph?","a":"<p>It compares the original and the summary and recommends improvements.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0173","card":"q-langgraph-039-6-1-design","sec":"langgraph-s023","q":"How are the edges set up in the reflection graph?","a":"<p>A conditional edge after the summarizer goes to the reviewer or END. <code>reviewer</code> to <code>summarizer</code> is a plain edge.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0174","card":"q-langgraph-039-6-1-design","sec":"langgraph-s023","q":"How are the reviewer and the summarizer given their roles?","a":"<p>With two system prompts. Both can share one model or use different ones.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0175","card":"q-langgraph-040-6-2-prompts","sec":"langgraph-s024","q":"What does the summarizer prompt ask for?","a":"<p>A summary with less than 50 words, and a revised version of its previous attempts when the user provides critique.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>For the input provided, create a summary with less than 50 words.\nIf the user has provides critique, responsed with a revised version of your previous attempts</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0176","card":"q-langgraph-040-6-2-prompts","sec":"langgraph-s024","q":"What does the reviewer prompt ask for?","a":"<p>Compare the user input document and the summary that was produced, check that the summary accurately reflects the document, and give recommendations in less than 50 words.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>Provide recommendations for improvement in less than 50 words.</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0177","card":"q-langgraph-040-6-2-prompts","sec":"langgraph-s024","q":"How can the summarizer and reviewer use the same or different models?","a":"<p>Option 1 uses <code>llm</code> for both. Option 2 uses different deployments, for example <code>gpt-4o</code> and <code>gpt-3.5-turbo</code>, for specialization.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>summarizer_llm = llm\nreviewer_llm = llm</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0178","card":"q-langgraph-041-6-3-the-agent","sec":"langgraph-s025","q":"What is the state of the reflection agent?","a":"<p><code>SummaryAgentState</code>, a <code>TypedDict</code> with <code>messages</code> using <code>Annotated[list[AnyMessage], operator.add]</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>class SummaryAgentState(TypedDict):\n    messages: Annotated[list[AnyMessage], operator.add]</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0179","card":"q-langgraph-041-6-3-the-agent","sec":"langgraph-s025","q":"How is the reflection graph wired in the <code>SummaryAgent</code>?","a":"<p>Nodes <code>summarizer</code> and <code>reviewer</code>. A conditional edge from <code>summarizer</code> maps <code>True</code> to <code>reviewer</code> and <code>False</code> to END. A plain edge goes from <code>reviewer</code> to <code>summarizer</code>. The entry point is <code>summarizer</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>summary_agent_graph.add_conditional_edges(\n    &quot;summarizer&quot;,\n    self.should_continue,\n    {True: &quot;reviewer&quot;, False: END }\n)\nsummary_agent_graph.add_edge(&quot;reviewer&quot;, &quot;summarizer&quot;)\nsummary_agent_graph.set_entry_point(&quot;summarizer&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0180","card":"q-langgraph-041-6-3-the-agent","sec":"langgraph-s025","q":"How do the summarizer and reviewer nodes use their prompts?","a":"<p>Each prepends its own system prompt to the message history, invokes the model, and returns the result as a new message.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>messages = [SystemMessage(content=self.summarizer_prompt)] + messages\nmessages = [SystemMessage(content=self.reviewer_prompt)] + messages</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0181","card":"q-langgraph-041-6-3-the-agent","sec":"langgraph-s025","q":"What does <code>should_continue</code> do in the reflection agent?","a":"<p>It returns <code>False</code> once the message list is longer than 4. Otherwise it returns <code>True</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>if len(state[&quot;messages&quot;]) &gt; 4:\n    return False\nelse:\n    return True</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0182","card":"q-langgraph-041-6-3-the-agent","sec":"langgraph-s025","q":"How many times do the summarizer and the reviewer run before the loop ends?","a":"<p>The summarizer runs 3 times and the reviewer 2 times.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0183","card":"q-langgraph-041-6-3-the-agent","sec":"langgraph-s025","q":"How does the lesson describe the iteration cap?","a":"<p>Three cycles, through <code>max_iterations = 3</code> and <code>(len(messages) - 1) // 2</code>. The notebook code comment says \"2 iterations\".</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0184","card":"q-langgraph-041-6-3-the-agent","sec":"langgraph-s025","q":"Does the reflection agent have conversation memory?","a":"<p>Yes. The graph compiles with <code>MemorySaver</code> as checkpointer.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>self.memory=MemorySaver()\nself.summary_agent_graph = summary_agent_graph.compile(checkpointer=self.memory)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0185","card":"q-langgraph-042-6-4-run-it","sec":"langgraph-s026","q":"What input does the reflection run use?","a":"<p>Page 1 of <code>data/EcoSprint_Specification_Document.pdf</code>, with newlines replaced by spaces.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>loader=PyPDFLoader(&quot;./data/EcoSprint_Specification_Document.pdf&quot;)\ndocs = loader.load()\nsource_content=docs[0].page_content.replace(&quot;\\n&quot;,&quot; &quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0186","card":"q-langgraph-042-6-4-run-it","sec":"langgraph-s026","q":"How do you create the summary chatbot with debug output and show its graph?","a":"<p>Create <code>SummaryAgent</code> with the model, both prompts and <code>debug=True</code>, then draw its graph.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>summary_chatbot = SummaryAgent(model, \n                               summarizer_prompt, \n                               reviewer_prompt,\n                               debug=True)\nImage(summary_chatbot.summary_agent_graph.get_graph().draw_mermaid_png())</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0187","card":"q-langgraph-042-6-4-run-it","sec":"langgraph-s026","q":"How do you execute a single reflection request?","a":"<p>Create a thread config, wrap the document in a <code>HumanMessage</code>, and invoke the graph.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>config = {&quot;configurable&quot;: {&quot;thread_id&quot;: str(uuid.uuid4())}}\nmessages=[HumanMessage(content=source_content)]\nresult=summary_chatbot.summary_agent_graph.invoke({&quot;messages&quot;:messages},config)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0188","card":"q-langgraph-043-6-5-human-in-the-loop-on-top-of-reflecti","sec":"langgraph-s027","q":"How does human-in-the-loop work on top of the reflection graph?","a":"<p>The thread keeps memory, so later user messages act as critique and re-enter the same loop. Each turn triggers several LLM calls, so it is slow.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0189","card":"q-langgraph-043-6-5-human-in-the-loop-on-top-of-reflecti","sec":"langgraph-s027","q":"What is the human-in-the-loop input sequence for the summarizer?","a":"<p>The source content, then \"Can you rewrite the review by focusing more on the specifications?\", then \"Can you remove details about the touchscreen?\", all on one thread.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>user_inputs = [\n    source_content,\n    &quot;Can you rewrite the review by focusing more on the specifications?&quot;,\n    &quot;Can you remove details about the touchscreen?&quot;\n]\nconfig = {&quot;configurable&quot;: {&quot;thread_id&quot;: &quot;thread-summarizer&quot;}}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0190","card":"q-langgraph-043-6-5-human-in-the-loop-on-top-of-reflecti","sec":"langgraph-s027","q":"How does <code>analyze_summary_quality</code> measure a summary?","a":"<p>It computes the compression ratio (summary length divided by original length) and the word count, and asks the LLM to rate accuracy, completeness, clarity and conciseness on a scale of 1 to 10.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>compression_ratio = len(summary) / len(original_text)\nword_count = len(summary.split())</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0191","card":"q-langgraph-044-7-1-design","sec":"langgraph-s028","q":"What is routing plus multi-agent in LangGraph?","a":"<p>A router classifies each request and hands it to a specialist, reusing agents already built.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0192","card":"q-langgraph-044-7-1-design","sec":"langgraph-s028","q":"What is the graph of the multi-agent chatbot?","a":"<p><code>Router</code> goes to <code>PRODUCT</code>, <code>ORDER</code>, <code>SMALLTALK</code> or <code>END</code>. Every destination goes to END. The routing is one-way, so control does not return to the router.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0193","card":"q-langgraph-044-7-1-design","sec":"langgraph-s028","q":"What are the nodes in the multi-agent chatbot?","a":"<p>Router: an LLM that classifies into one word. Product_Agent: the Product Q&amp;A agent. Orders_Agent: the custom Orders agent. Small_Talk: an LLM with a small-talk prompt.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0194","card":"q-langgraph-044-7-1-design","sec":"langgraph-s028","q":"How does the conditional edge in the router graph pick a node?","a":"<p>It maps the router's output text straight to a node name.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0195","card":"q-langgraph-045-7-2-reusing-agents-as-nodes","sec":"langgraph-s029","q":"How does the multi-agent notebook reuse the Product Q&amp;A and Orders agents?","a":"<p>Notebook 06 imports the earlier notebooks with <code>%run</code>. This also executes their chatbot cells, so ignore that output.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>%run &quot;code_03_XX Product QnA Agentic chatbot.ipynb&quot; \n%run &quot;code_04_XX Orders Chatbot with custom agent.ipynb&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0196","card":"q-langgraph-045-7-2-reusing-agents-as-nodes","sec":"langgraph-s029","q":"What does the <code>agent_node</code> helper do?","a":"<p>It reads <code>thread_id</code> from the router's run config and passes it to the inner agent, keeping each agent's memory tied to the conversation. It returns the agent's last message as an <code>AIMessage</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>thread_id=config[&quot;metadata&quot;][&quot;thread_id&quot;]\nagent_config = {&quot;configurable&quot;: {&quot;thread_id&quot;: thread_id}}\nresult = agent.invoke(state, agent_config)\nfinal_result=AIMessage(result[&#x27;messages&#x27;][-1].content)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0197","card":"q-langgraph-045-7-2-reusing-agents-as-nodes","sec":"langgraph-s029","q":"What does <code>functools.partial</code> do for the agent nodes?","a":"<p>It pre-binds <code>agent</code> and <code>name</code>, leaving <code>(state, config)</code> for LangGraph.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>product_QnA_node=functools.partial(agent_node, \n                                   agent=product_QnA_agent, \n                                   name=&quot;Product_QnA_Agent&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0198","card":"q-langgraph-045-7-2-reusing-agents-as-nodes","sec":"langgraph-s029","q":"How is the custom Orders agent passed to <code>agent_node</code>?","a":"<p>By its graph: <code>orders_agent.agent_graph</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>orders_node=functools.partial(agent_node,\n                              agent=orders_agent.agent_graph,\n                              name=&quot;Orders_Agent&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0199","card":"q-langgraph-046-7-3-router-agent","sec":"langgraph-s030","q":"How is the router graph built in LangGraph?","a":"<p>Nodes <code>Router</code>, <code>Product_Agent</code>, <code>Orders_Agent</code> and <code>Small_Talk</code>, with conditional edges from <code>Router</code> that map <code>PRODUCT</code>, <code>ORDER</code>, <code>SMALLTALK</code> and <code>END</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>router_graph.add_conditional_edges(\n    &quot;Router&quot;,\n    self.find_route,\n    {&quot;PRODUCT&quot;: &quot;Product_Agent&quot;, \n     &quot;ORDER&quot; : &quot;Orders_Agent&quot;,\n     &quot;SMALLTALK&quot; : &quot;Small_Talk&quot;,\n     &quot;END&quot;: END }\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0200","card":"q-langgraph-046-7-3-router-agent","sec":"langgraph-s030","q":"How do the specialist nodes end in the router graph?","a":"<p>Each has a plain edge to END, which is one-way routing that does not come back to the router.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>router_graph.add_edge(&quot;Product_Agent&quot;,END)\nrouter_graph.add_edge(&quot;Orders_Agent&quot;,END)\nrouter_graph.add_edge(&quot;Small_Talk&quot;,END)\nrouter_graph.set_entry_point(&quot;Router&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0201","card":"q-langgraph-046-7-3-router-agent","sec":"langgraph-s030","q":"Does the router graph have a checkpointer, and where does memory live?","a":"<p>No. Memory lives in the inner agents, through the forwarded thread ID.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0202","card":"q-langgraph-046-7-3-router-agent","sec":"langgraph-s030","q":"What does <code>find_route</code> return in the notebook router?","a":"<p>The last message content, the LLM text, as the route key. Prompt wording and dictionary keys must match exactly.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>destination=last_message.content\nreturn destination</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0203","card":"q-langgraph-046-7-3-router-agent","sec":"langgraph-s030","q":"What does the <code>Small_Talk</code> node do?","a":"<p>It prepends the small-talk system prompt to the messages and invokes the model.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>messages = [SystemMessage(content=self.smalltalk_prompt)] + messages\nresult = self.model.invoke(messages)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0204","card":"q-langgraph-047-7-3-router-agent","sec":"langgraph-s030","q":"What does the router system prompt tell the model?","a":"<p>Choose one of 4 options: SMALLTALK (greetings and goodbyes), PRODUCT (laptop features, specifications and pricing), ORDER (order status, details or quantity update), END (default). Output only one word.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>The output should only be just one word out of the possible 4 : SMALLTALK, PRODUCT, ORDER, END.</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0205","card":"q-langgraph-047-7-3-router-agent","sec":"langgraph-s030","q":"What does the small-talk prompt tell the model to do?","a":"<p>Respond professionally to greetings and goodbyes, and mention that it can answer laptop product feature questions and give order status and updates.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0206","card":"q-langgraph-047-7-3-router-agent","sec":"langgraph-s030","q":"How do you create the router agent and show its graph?","a":"<p>Pass the model, the system prompt, the small-talk prompt and <code>debug</code>, then draw the graph.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>router_agent = RouterAgent(model, \n                           system_prompt, \n                           smalltalk_prompt,\n                           debug=False)\nImage(router_agent.router_graph.get_graph().draw_mermaid_png())</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0207","card":"q-langgraph-047-7-3-router-agent","sec":"langgraph-s030","q":"How does the lesson's more forgiving <code>find_route</code> work?","a":"<p>It lower-cases and strips the LLM output, matches by substring (\"product\", \"order\", \"small_talk\" or \"small talk\"), uses lower-case keys, and falls back to \"end\".</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>route_decision = last_message.content.lower().strip()\n\nif &quot;product&quot; in route_decision:\n    return &quot;product&quot;\nelif &quot;order&quot; in route_decision:\n    return &quot;order&quot;\nelse:\n    return &quot;end&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0208","card":"q-langgraph-048-7-4-execution","sec":"langgraph-s031","q":"How do you run a single request through the router?","a":"<p>Build a <code>HumanMessage</code> list and call <code>router_agent.router_graph.invoke</code>. The result shows the router message, then the specialist's reply.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>messages=[HumanMessage(content=&quot;What is the status of order ORD-7311?&quot;)]\nresult=router_agent.router_graph.invoke({&quot;messages&quot;:messages},config)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0209","card":"q-langgraph-048-7-4-execution","sec":"langgraph-s031","q":"Why do follow-ups like \"add one more of that laptop\" and \"How much does it cost?\" work through the router?","a":"<p>Each inner agent keeps memory under the shared thread ID.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0210","card":"q-langgraph-048-7-4-execution","sec":"langgraph-s031","q":"How do you run a full conversation through the router?","a":"<p>Create one thread config, loop over the inputs, and call <code>router_agent.router_graph.invoke</code> with the same config.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>config = {&quot;configurable&quot;: {&quot;thread_id&quot;: str(uuid.uuid4())}}\nai_response = router_agent.router_graph.invoke(user_message,config=config)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0211","card":"q-langgraph-049-7-5-extras-from-the-lesson-file","sec":"langgraph-s032","q":"What does <code>analyze_routing_patterns</code> do?","a":"<p>It counts routing decisions across sample requests. It sends each request through the router, reads the router decision from the second message, and counts product, order and small_talk.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>route = result[&quot;messages&quot;][1].content.lower()  # Router decision</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0212","card":"q-langgraph-049-7-5-extras-from-the-lesson-file","sec":"langgraph-s032","q":"What does <code>DynamicRouterAgent.register_agent</code> do?","a":"<p>It registers agents at runtime: stores the agent by route keyword, adds a node and an edge to END, and recompiles the graph.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>self.agent_graph.add_node(agent_name.lower(), agent_node_func)\nself.agent_graph.add_edge(agent_name.lower(), END)\n\nself.compiled_graph = self.agent_graph.compile()</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0213","card":"q-langgraph-049-7-5-extras-from-the-lesson-file","sec":"langgraph-s032","q":"How does <code>DynamicRouterAgent.find_route</code> choose a route?","a":"<p>It checks registered keywords first, then falls back to the default routing from the parent class.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>return super().find_route(state)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0214","card":"q-langgraph-050-8-beyond-langgraph-other-frameworks-tool","sec":"langgraph-s033","q":"What is covered in the closing lesson of the LangGraph course?","a":"<p>Other frameworks, advanced tools, and a production shape for agents. The snippets are illustrative, with placeholder keys and undefined helpers.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0215","card":"q-langgraph-051-8-1-same-agent-idea-in-other-frameworks","sec":"langgraph-s034","q":"How do LangGraph, LlamaIndex, AutoGen and CrewAI differ?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Framework</th><th>Core idea</th><th>Main objects</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>LangGraph</td><td>Explicit graph of nodes/edges with shared state</td><td><code>StateGraph</code>, <code>create_react_agent</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td>LlamaIndex</td><td>Index/RAG-centric agents</td><td><code>ReActAgent</code>, <code>FunctionTool</code>, <code>VectorStoreIndex</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td>AutoGen</td><td>Conversational multi-agent chats</td><td><code>AssistantAgent</code>, <code>UserProxyAgent</code>, <code>GroupChat</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td>CrewAI</td><td>Role-based teams with tasks</td><td><code>Agent</code>, <code>Task</code>, <code>Crew</code></td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0216","card":"q-langgraph-051-8-1-same-agent-idea-in-other-frameworks","sec":"langgraph-s034","q":"In LlamaIndex, how do you build a ReAct agent with a function tool?","a":"<p>Wrap a function with <code>FunctionTool.from_defaults</code>, then create <code>ReActAgent.from_tools</code> with the tool and an LLM, and call <code>chat</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>multiply_tool = FunctionTool.from_defaults(fn=multiply)\n\nllm = OpenAI(model=&quot;gpt-3.5-turbo&quot;)\nagent = ReActAgent.from_tools([multiply_tool], llm=llm, verbose=True)\n\nresponse = agent.chat(&quot;What is 21 multiplied by 2?&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0217","card":"q-langgraph-051-8-1-same-agent-idea-in-other-frameworks","sec":"langgraph-s034","q":"In LlamaIndex, how do you make a ReAct chat engine from documents?","a":"<p>Load documents with <code>SimpleDirectoryReader</code>, build a <code>VectorStoreIndex</code>, and call <code>as_chat_engine</code> with <code>chat_mode=\"react\"</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>documents = SimpleDirectoryReader(&quot;research_papers/&quot;).load_data()\n\nindex = VectorStoreIndex.from_documents(documents)\n\nagent = index.as_chat_engine(chat_mode=&quot;react&quot;, verbose=True)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0218","card":"q-langgraph-052-8-1-same-agent-idea-in-other-frameworks","sec":"langgraph-s034","q":"In AutoGen, how do you set up conversational agents?","a":"<p>Create an <code>AssistantAgent</code> with an <code>llm_config</code>, and a <code>UserProxyAgent</code> with <code>human_input_mode=\"NEVER\"</code> and a <code>code_execution_config</code>. Then call <code>initiate_chat</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>assistant = autogen.AssistantAgent(\n    name=&quot;assistant&quot;,\n    llm_config={&quot;config_list&quot;: config_list}\n)\n\nuser_proxy = autogen.UserProxyAgent(\n    name=&quot;user_proxy&quot;,\n    human_input_mode=&quot;NEVER&quot;,\n    code_execution_config={&quot;work_dir&quot;: &quot;coding&quot;}\n)\n\nuser_proxy.initiate_chat(\n    assistant,\n    message=&quot;Create a Python function to calculate fibonacci numbers&quot;\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0219","card":"q-langgraph-052-8-1-same-agent-idea-in-other-frameworks","sec":"langgraph-s034","q":"In CrewAI, how do you build a team of agents?","a":"<p>Define <code>Agent</code> objects with role, goal and backstory, define <code>Task</code> objects with a description and an agent, create a <code>Crew</code> with the agents and tasks, and call <code>kickoff()</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>crew = Crew(\n    agents=[researcher, writer],\n    tasks=[research_task, writing_task],\n    verbose=2\n)\n\nresult = crew.kickoff()</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0220","card":"q-langgraph-052-8-1-same-agent-idea-in-other-frameworks","sec":"langgraph-s034","q":"In CrewAI, what do the researcher and writer agents look like?","a":"<p>The researcher has role 'Research Analyst'. The writer has role 'Content Writer'. Each has a goal and a backstory.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>researcher = Agent(\n    role=&#x27;Research Analyst&#x27;,\n    goal=&#x27;Gather comprehensive information on given topics&#x27;,\n    backstory=&#x27;Expert at finding and analyzing information&#x27;,\n    verbose=True\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0221","card":"q-langgraph-052-8-1-same-agent-idea-in-other-frameworks","sec":"langgraph-s034","q":"In AutoGen, how do you create a reviewer group chat?","a":"<p>Define specialized <code>AssistantAgent</code>s, such as a code reviewer and a security expert, and put them in an <code>autogen.GroupChat</code> with <code>max_round=10</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>group_chat = autogen.GroupChat(\n    agents=[code_reviewer, security_expert],\n    messages=[],\n    max_round=10\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0222","card":"q-langgraph-053-8-2-advanced-tools","sec":"langgraph-s035","q":"What is multi-source RAG as a tool?","a":"<p>Several vector stores, plus one function that queries all of them and merges labeled results.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0223","card":"q-langgraph-053-8-2-advanced-tools","sec":"langgraph-s035","q":"How does the <code>AdvancedRAGAgent</code> set up its knowledge bases?","a":"<p>It loads web content with <code>WebBaseLoader</code> and a PDF with <code>PDFLoader</code>, and creates a separate Chroma vector store for each.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>self.vectorstores[&quot;web&quot;] = Chroma.from_documents(web_docs, self.embeddings)\nself.vectorstores[&quot;docs&quot;] = Chroma.from_documents(pdf_docs, self.embeddings)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0224","card":"q-langgraph-053-8-2-advanced-tools","sec":"langgraph-s035","q":"How does <code>multi_source_search</code> query the knowledge bases?","a":"<p>It loops over the vector stores and runs <code>similarity_search</code> with <code>k=3</code> on each, storing results by source name.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>for source, vectorstore in self.vectorstores.items():\n    results[source] = vectorstore.similarity_search(query, k=3)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0225","card":"q-langgraph-053-8-2-advanced-tools","sec":"langgraph-s035","q":"How does the <code>advanced_rag_search</code> tool combine results?","a":"<p>It labels each document with its source in brackets and joins them with newlines.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>combined_context.append(f&quot;[{source}] {doc.page_content}&quot;)\n\nreturn &quot;\\n&quot;.join(combined_context)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0226","card":"q-langgraph-054-8-2-advanced-tools","sec":"langgraph-s035","q":"What third-party API tools does the closing lesson show?","a":"<p>A weather tool, a Slack notification tool and a read-only SQL database tool.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0227","card":"q-langgraph-054-8-2-advanced-tools","sec":"langgraph-s035","q":"How does <code>weather_api_tool</code> work?","a":"<p>It builds an OpenWeatherMap URL with the location and an API key, calls it with <code>requests.get</code>, and returns the description and temperature in kelvin if the status is 200. Otherwise it returns a failure message.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>response = requests.get(url)\nif response.status_code == 200:\n    data = response.json()\n    return f&quot;Weather in {location}: {data[&#x27;weather&#x27;][0][&#x27;description&#x27;]}, {data[&#x27;main&#x27;][&#x27;temp&#x27;]}K&quot;\nreturn f&quot;Could not fetch weather for {location}&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0228","card":"q-langgraph-054-8-2-advanced-tools","sec":"langgraph-s035","q":"How does <code>slack_notification_tool</code> send a message?","a":"<p>It posts a payload with the channel, text and username \"AI Agent\" to a webhook URL with <code>requests.post</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>payload = {\n    &quot;channel&quot;: channel,\n    &quot;text&quot;: message,\n    &quot;username&quot;: &quot;AI Agent&quot;\n}\n\nresponse = requests.post(webhook_url, json=payload)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0229","card":"q-langgraph-054-8-2-advanced-tools","sec":"langgraph-s035","q":"How does <code>database_query_tool</code> stay safe?","a":"<p>It only allows queries that start with <code>SELECT</code>. Anything else returns \"Only SELECT queries are allowed\". It also closes the connection in a <code>finally</code> block.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>if query.strip().upper().startswith(&quot;SELECT&quot;):\n    cursor.execute(query)\n    results = cursor.fetchall()\n    return str(results)\nelse:\n    return &quot;Only SELECT queries are allowed&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0230","card":"q-langgraph-055-8-3-production-shape-config-logging-metr","sec":"langgraph-s036","q":"What does <code>AgentConfig</code> hold in the enterprise agent template?","a":"<p><code>name</code>, <code>description</code>, <code>tools</code>, <code>max_iterations</code> (default 10), <code>timeout_seconds</code> (default 300) and <code>log_level</code> (default \"INFO\").</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>@dataclass\nclass AgentConfig:\n    name: str\n    description: str\n    tools: List[str]\n    max_iterations: int = 10\n    timeout_seconds: int = 300\n    log_level: str = &quot;INFO&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0231","card":"q-langgraph-055-8-3-production-shape-config-logging-metr","sec":"langgraph-s036","q":"What metrics does <code>EnterpriseAgent</code> keep?","a":"<p><code>requests_processed</code>, <code>errors_encountered</code> and <code>average_response_time</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>self.metrics = {\n    &quot;requests_processed&quot;: 0,\n    &quot;errors_encountered&quot;: 0,\n    &quot;average_response_time&quot;: 0\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0232","card":"q-langgraph-055-8-3-production-shape-config-logging-metr","sec":"langgraph-s036","q":"How does <code>EnterpriseAgent</code> set up logging?","a":"<p>It creates a logger named after the agent, sets the level from the config, and adds a <code>StreamHandler</code> with a formatter of time, name, level and message.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>logger = logging.getLogger(self.config.name)\nlogger.setLevel(getattr(logging, self.config.log_level))\n\nhandler = logging.StreamHandler()</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0233","card":"q-langgraph-055-8-3-production-shape-config-logging-metr","sec":"langgraph-s036","q":"What does <code>EnterpriseAgent.setup_agent</code> do?","a":"<p>It loads tools from the config, sets up monitoring, and creates the LangGraph agent.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>self.tools = self.load_tools(self.config.tools)\n\nself.setup_monitoring()\n\nself.agent = self.create_langgraph_agent()</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0234","card":"q-langgraph-055-8-3-production-shape-config-logging-metr","sec":"langgraph-s036","q":"How does <code>process_request</code> handle success and failure?","a":"<p>On success it increments <code>requests_processed</code> and returns <code>success</code>, <code>response</code>, <code>response_time</code> and <code>user_id</code>. On an exception it increments <code>errors_encountered</code>, logs the error, and returns <code>success: False</code> with the error.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>self.metrics[&quot;requests_processed&quot;] += 1\nresponse_time = (datetime.now() - start_time).total_seconds()</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0235","card":"q-langgraph-056-8-3-production-shape-config-logging-metr","sec":"langgraph-s036","q":"How does the closing lesson serve an agent over HTTP?","a":"<p>With FastAPI. A <code>POST /chat</code> endpoint takes a <code>ChatRequest</code> and returns a <code>ChatResponse</code>, and <code>GET /metrics</code> returns the agent's metrics.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>@app.post(&quot;/chat&quot;, response_model=ChatResponse)\nasync def chat_endpoint(request: ChatRequest):\n\n@app.get(&quot;/metrics&quot;)\nasync def get_metrics():\n    return enterprise_agent.metrics</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0236","card":"q-langgraph-056-8-3-production-shape-config-logging-metr","sec":"langgraph-s036","q":"What fields do the request and response models have in the FastAPI example?","a":"<p><code>ChatRequest</code> has <code>message</code>, <code>user_id</code> and an optional <code>session_id</code>. <code>ChatResponse</code> has <code>response</code>, <code>session_id</code> and <code>processing_time</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>class ChatRequest(BaseModel):\n    message: str\n    user_id: str\n    session_id: Optional[str] = None\n\nclass ChatResponse(BaseModel):\n    response: str\n    session_id: str\n    processing_time: float</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0237","card":"q-langgraph-056-8-3-production-shape-config-logging-metr","sec":"langgraph-s036","q":"What does the <code>/chat</code> endpoint do when the agent fails?","a":"<p>It raises <code>HTTPException</code> with status 500 and the error as the detail.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>raise HTTPException(status_code=500, detail=result[&quot;error&quot;])</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0238","card":"q-langgraph-056-8-3-production-shape-config-logging-metr","sec":"langgraph-s036","q":"How is the FastAPI server started?","a":"<p>With <code>uvicorn.run(app, host=\"0.0.0.0\", port=8000)</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>uvicorn.run(app, host=&quot;0.0.0.0&quot;, port=8000)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0239","card":"q-langgraph-056-8-3-production-shape-config-logging-metr","sec":"langgraph-s036","q":"What does the enterprise readiness checklist cover?","a":"<p>Security (authN/authZ, encryption, audit logging), scalability (load balancing, DB optimization, caching), monitoring (metrics, error alerting, usage analytics), and integration (legacy systems, third-party APIs, data pipelines).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0240","card":"q-langgraph-056-8-3-production-shape-config-logging-metr","sec":"langgraph-s036","q":"What next steps does the course name?","a":"<p>LlamaIndex, AutoGen, CrewAI, then RAG/API tools, then production agents. Later topics include multi-modal agents, agent safety and evaluation metrics.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0241","card":"q-langgraph-057-9-gotchas-version-notes","sec":"langgraph-s037","q":"Why do versions matter in the LangGraph course?","a":"<p>The notebooks pin <code>langgraph==0.2.59</code> and <code>langchain==0.3.12</code>. In that version <code>create_react_agent(..., state_modifier=...)</code> is the argument name. Newer LangGraph releases renamed it to <code>prompt</code>. Match the pinned versions when running the course code.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0242","card":"q-langgraph-057-9-gotchas-version-notes","sec":"langgraph-s037","q":"Why are tool docstrings important in LangGraph?","a":"<p>They are the tool's API for the LLM. Vague docstrings give wrong tool choices. A retriever tool's <code>description</code> plays the same role.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0243","card":"q-langgraph-057-9-gotchas-version-notes","sec":"langgraph-s037","q":"What return convention do the course tools use for \"not found\"?","a":"<p><code>-1</code>, so the LLM can tell the user clearly.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0244","card":"q-langgraph-057-9-gotchas-version-notes","sec":"langgraph-s037","q":"What does <code>Annotated[list, operator.add]</code> do in LangGraph state, and what happens without a reducer?","a":"<p>It makes state updates append. Without a reducer, a node's return value replaces the field.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0245","card":"q-langgraph-057-9-gotchas-version-notes","sec":"langgraph-s037","q":"What is a thread ID in LangGraph, and what are the limits of <code>MemorySaver</code>?","a":"<p>Thread ID is the conversation. <code>MemorySaver</code> is in-process and lost on restart. Reuse the same <code>thread_id</code> for follow-ups and use a new one per user conversation.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0246","card":"q-langgraph-057-9-gotchas-version-notes","sec":"langgraph-s037","q":"Which graph has no checkpointer in the course, and how does it get memory?","a":"<p>The router graph. It forwards the thread ID to the inner agents, which keep the memory.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0247","card":"q-langgraph-057-9-gotchas-version-notes","sec":"langgraph-s037","q":"Why cap loops in LangGraph agents?","a":"<p>ReAct and reflection both loop. Use an iteration limit (<code>max_iterations</code>, a message-count check) to avoid infinite cycles.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0248","card":"q-langgraph-057-9-gotchas-version-notes","sec":"langgraph-s037","q":"What is the router prompt and key coupling gotcha?","a":"<p>A router that returns raw LLM text as the edge key breaks on any wording drift. Constrain the output to one word, or normalize in <code>find_route</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0249","card":"q-langgraph-057-9-gotchas-version-notes","sec":"langgraph-s037","q":"What is the difference between streaming and <code>invoke</code> in LangGraph?","a":"<p><code>stream(..., stream_mode=\"values\")</code> shows each step as it happens. <code>invoke</code> returns only the final state.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langgraph-f0250","card":"q-langgraph-057-9-gotchas-version-notes","sec":"langgraph-s037","q":"What notebook quirks does the LangGraph course list?","a":"<p><code>call_tools</code> returns inside its <code>for</code> loop and handles only the first tool call. Chunk settings differ between lesson (<code>overlap=100</code>, <code>k=3</code>) and notebook (<code>overlap=256</code>, <code>k=1</code>). The notebooks contain a hard-coded Azure key, so use your own environment variables.</p>","hand":true}];
